/**
 * Long-form hospital descriptions compiled from each hospital's public website and
 * other public web sources. Sections start with a "##key" line (history,
 * specialities, technology, international); figures the sources disagreed on
 * are left out or described as approximate.
 */
export const hospitalAbout: Record<string, string> = {
	'moolchand-hospital':
		"##history\nMoolchand Kharaiti Ram Hospital, now known as Moolchand Medcity, has served patients in Delhi for around six decades and has grown into a multispeciality group with facilities in South Delhi and Agra. Over the years it built a reputation for pioneering work: it was the first hospital in India to introduce streptokinase therapy for heart attacks and to perform minimal-access surgery, and it was among the first multispeciality hospitals to offer laparoscopic and thoracoscopic procedures. It has also received the International Asia Pacific Quality Award and the Rajiv Gandhi National Quality Commendation Certificate in the healthcare category.\n##specialities\nThe South Delhi centre brings together more than 250 doctors across over 50 specialities. Departments include emergency and urgent care, critical care, renal care and dialysis, gastroenterology and hepatology, general and advanced laparoscopic surgery, heart care, neurosciences, orthopaedics, paediatrics, Ayurveda and a dedicated women's institute. Its orthopaedic institute covers bone, joint, spine, trauma and sports injuries, with internationally trained surgeons, and the hospital also provides cardiology, neurosurgery, obstetrics and gynaecology, respiratory medicine, urology, oncology, ENT and ophthalmology.\n##technology\nMoolchand is known for well-equipped surgical theatres, intensive care units and specialty clinics, supported by comprehensive diagnostic imaging and laboratory services. The hospital holds JCI, NABH, NABL and ISO 9001 accreditation, and has maintained JCI accreditation over multiple cycles, something only a handful of Indian hospitals have achieved.\n##international\nPatients and families from more than 50 countries use Moolchand's services, and the hospital reports performing thousands of surgeries each year for international patients. It provides translators and interpreters and a dedicated international patient service. Its central South Delhi location near Lajpat Nagar makes it convenient to combine treatment with accommodation nearby.",
	'fortis-c-doc-hospital':
		"##history\nFortis C-DOC Hospital for Diabetes and Allied Sciences has operated since 2011–2012 as a centre of excellence for diabetes, metabolic diseases and endocrine disorders. It is led by Prof. (Dr.) Anoop Misra, a former professor of medicine at AIIMS, recipient of the Dr. B. C. Roy Award and the Padma Shri, and the director of the National Diabetes, Obesity and Cholesterol Foundation. The hospital was named Best Hospital in India in Diabetes Care at the CIMS Healthcare Excellence Awards for several consecutive years between 2014 and 2018.\n##specialities\nThe hospital focuses on comprehensive management of diabetes and its complications, along with obesity, thyroid and other endocrine conditions. It runs an advanced centre for diabetic foot and wound care, scientific weight-loss and weight-management programmes, and bariatric and minimal-access surgery. It also provides expertise in general surgery, orthopaedics, gastroenterology, ENT, pain management and urology.\n##technology\nThe facility is a compact 23-bed hospital spread over about 20,000 square feet, with two operating suites, a diabetic eye lab and a dialysis centre. Clinicians are supported by a diagnostic laboratory, radiology and pharmacy services that operate around the clock.\n##international\nFortis C-DOC states that it is keen to work with foreign institutions and scientists on exchange of ideas, education and collaborative research. For international patients, it offers a focused, single-specialty setting for long-term diabetes and metabolic care, including foot care and weight management. Located in Chirag Enclave opposite Nehru Place, it is easily reached from South Delhi hotels.",
	'fortis-escorts-heart-institute':
		"##history\nFortis Escorts Heart Institute in Okhla was established in 1988 and has become one of India's best-known cardiac hospitals. In 2013 it celebrated 25 years of cardiac care, and it reports more than 200,000 cardiac surgeries and 350,000 cath-lab interventions to date. The institute was founded by cardiac surgeon Dr. Naresh Trehan, who returned to India from the United States to start it, and it now operates as part of Fortis Healthcare.\n##specialities\nThe hospital provides advanced cardiac care in complex angioplasty, transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR), cardiac pacing and electrophysiology, adult cardiac surgery, aortic aneurysm repair, LVAD support, heart transplantation, minimally invasive cardiac surgery, robotic surgery, and paediatric cardiology and cardiac surgery. It is also recognised for its work on gastrointestinal, pancreatic and liver disorders, including liver transplants and auto-liver transplants.\n##technology\nA 310-bed multispeciality hospital, Fortis Escorts combines dedicated cath labs, cardiac operating theatres and critical care units with the diagnostic and imaging services needed for complex heart cases. It is described as one of the leading heart hospitals in Delhi for open-heart surgery, heart failure care and heart transplantation.\n##international\nThe hospital treats a large number of international patients every year and has experience across all modalities of cardiac care, which is important for patients who need a definitive diagnosis, surgery and structured follow-up in one place. Its Okhla Road location, opposite Sukhdev Vihar Metro Station, is well connected to South Delhi and the airport.",
	'fortis-flt-lt-rajan-dhall-hospital':
		"##history\nFortis Flt. Lt. Rajan Dhall Hospital in Vasant Kunj opened in 2006 and is a 162+ bed multispeciality hospital in South Delhi. It has treated more than two million patients across about 30 specialised fields and reports over 8,500 complex gastrointestinal surgeries and more than 9,300 joint replacements. It received a nursing excellence award from AHPI in 2018, a CII silver award for energy management in 2018, and was featured in Newsweek's World's Best Hospitals list for 2022.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers dedicated centres in cardiac sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, oncology, rheumatology, pulmonology and critical care, and bariatric sciences, alongside neurosciences, gastroenterology and urology. Its specialised clinics include asthma and allergy, kidney stone, obesity, sports injury and a menopause clinic, and it supports several clinical verticals such as endocrinology, dermatology, diabetology, infertility and sports medicine.\n##technology\nThe hospital uses robotic platforms including the da Vinci system and other robotic systems for minimally invasive surgery and robotic knee replacement, together with advanced neuro-microscopy for brain and spine surgery. Diagnostics range from blood, hormonal and thyroid testing to ECG, echocardiography, TMT, X-ray, ultrasound, mammography, DEXA and endoscopy. It is accredited by NABH and NABL and holds nursing excellence certification.\n##international\nPatients from more than 50 countries choose this hospital, partly because it is only about 8 km from the international airport. International patients receive support services intended to make the stay comfortable.",
	'blk-max-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nBLK-Max Super Speciality Hospital is one of the largest private tertiary-care hospitals in India, set on about five acres in the Pusa Road area of central Delhi with a legacy dating back to 1959. Today it operates with Max Healthcare and has 650 beds. Among its milestones, it is described as India's first private hospital with a dual-console robotic surgical system, and the first in Asia and seventh in the world to install the CyberKnife VSI radiosurgery platform. It has won awards including the ET Healthworld award for best multispeciality hospital and the AHPI award for Quality Beyond Accreditation.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has dedicated centres for cancer, bone marrow transplant, heart, neurosciences, digestive and liver diseases, renal sciences and kidney transplant, bone, joint and spine, chest and respiratory diseases, and critical care. It runs a robust programme for bone marrow, liver, kidney and heart transplants and is known for one of North India's largest bone marrow transplant centres, with sub-programmes including autologous, allogeneic, haploidentical, cord blood and matched-unrelated-donor transplants. It is also a leader in neuro-endovascular procedures.\n##technology\nWith 650 beds, about 162 critical care beds and 22 modular operation theatres, the hospital is equipped for complex multi-organ care. It holds JCI, NABH and NABL accreditation.\n##international\nBLK-Max reports treating more than 20,000 international patients a year from over 80 countries, with a dedicated international patient services team and a personal coordinator assigned to each patient. Its central location near Rajendra Place Metro makes it well connected.",
	'artemis-hospital':
		"##history\nArtemis Hospital in Sector 51, Gurugram, was launched in 2007 by the promoters of the Apollo Tyres Group and is described as the first hospital in Gurugram to be accredited by JCI and NABH. It has achieved JCI accreditation multiple times and has been recognised with the Asia Pacific Hand Hygiene Excellence Award from the World Health Organization (2016) and an infection-control excellence award from the Quality Council of India (2019). It is led by Dr. Devlina Chakravarty as Managing Director.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has more than 600 beds and specialists in over 40 disciplines, with integrated care in cardiology and cardiac surgery, oncology, neurology and neurosurgery, orthopaedics, nephrology, gastroenterology, pulmonology, urology, emergency medicine and organ transplantation. Its neurosciences centre treats stroke, brain tumours and movement disorders, and offers Gamma Knife radiosurgery, deep brain stimulation, spine instrumentation and neuro-rehabilitation.\n##technology\nArtemis stands on a modern 9-acre campus and uses the da Vinci robotic surgical system for minimally invasive procedures. Its joint replacement and orthopaedic centre offers robotic-assisted knee, hip and shoulder procedures and sports-injury treatment using minimally invasive methods.\n##international\nArtemis presents itself as a JCI and NABH accredited hospital with advanced care for international patients. Its Golf Course Road-side location in Gurugram is close to hotels and about half an hour from the international airport in normal traffic.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-saket':
		"##history\nMax Super Speciality Hospital, Saket, began operating in 2001 and has grown into a hospital of over 500 beds in South Delhi, arranged as East and West blocks. Across the two wings it has treated more than 3.4 million patients in over 30 specialities. It carries the distinction of installing Asia's first and the world's third intra-operative MRI suite (BrainSuite), and it offers several technologies described as firsts in India and Asia.\n##specialities\nThe East wing specialises in cardiac care, oncology (medical, surgical and radiotherapy), transplants (heart, lung and bone marrow) and general surgery including minimal-access and bariatric procedures, and the hospital is accredited as a centre of excellence for bariatric and hernia surgery. Across the campus, 680+ specialists cover cardiology, orthopaedics, urology, neurology, neurosurgery, gastroenterology and organ transplants, among others.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 25 high-end modular operation theatres, 170+ critical care beds, a dedicated endoscopy unit, an advanced dialysis unit and an onco day-care unit, along with an emergency resuscitation and observation unit. It holds JCI and NABH accreditation.\n##international\nMax Saket receives patients from over 130 countries and reports treating more than 300,000 international patients. Its dedicated international patient services cover treatment planning, medical opinions, visa assistance, airport pickup, interpreters, accommodation support and post-treatment follow-up. Located in the Saket district near a Metro station and shopping centres, it is convenient for patients and families.",
	'indraprastha-apollo-hospitals':
		"##history\nIndraprastha Apollo Hospitals, opened in 1996 in Sarita Vihar, is the flagship Apollo hospital in Delhi, spread over 15 acres with about 710 operational beds and more than 250 ICU beds. It was the first hospital in India to be accredited by JCI (in 2005) and has been re-accredited since. It performed India's first successful paediatric liver transplant in 1998 and is one of the world's busiest solid-organ transplant centres. It has been featured in Newsweek's World's Best Hospitals and has received medical value travel awards.\n##specialities\nThe hospital runs one of India's busiest liver and kidney transplant programmes and a dedicated bone marrow transplant unit, along with multi-organ transplants including heart, pancreas, intestine and paediatric cases. Its comprehensive cancer centre offers advanced radiation therapy including HDR brachytherapy and tomotherapy, and it is home to India's first proton therapy centre. Other strengths include cardiac sciences, neurosciences, orthopaedics and gastroenterology.\n##technology\nThe hospital offers the da Vinci robotic surgical system and advanced radiotherapy platforms, supported by extensive critical care capacity.\n##international\nThe hospital handles close to 200,000 patients a year, of whom around 9,500 are international, from countries including the United States, Australia, Malaysia, Yemen, Brunei and Tanzania. Its Sarita Vihar location on the Delhi–Mathura Road is well connected to South Delhi and the airport.",
	'apollo-spectra-hospitals':
		"##history\nApollo Spectra Hospitals is the Apollo group's network of hospitals focused on surgical and day-care specialities. In Delhi it operates two centres: one at Plot 3, Block 34, Pusa Road in Karol Bagh, and another at Plot A-2, Outer Ring Road, Chirag Enclave near Greater Kailash-1. Together they bring the Apollo name to focused surgical care in central and South Delhi.\n##specialities\nThe centres offer general and laparoscopic surgery, orthopaedics and spine, urology, varicose veins, bariatric surgery, gynaecology and ENT, and also perform procedures in ophthalmology, paediatrics, plastic and cosmetic surgery and radiology. The Karol Bagh centre has more than 130 healthcare professionals and about 60 specialist consultants, while the Chirag Enclave centre has over 120 professionals including about 65 specialist consultants.\n##technology\nThe Karol Bagh hospital has a state-of-the-art endoscopy suite, modern modular operating theatres and an advanced critical care unit. The Chirag Enclave hospital has modular operating theatres, a rehabilitation unit, an in-house pharmacy and a family waiting area for inpatients. Both centres have pharmacies, pathology laboratories, radiology and ambulance services.\n##international\nBecause Apollo Spectra focuses on planned surgery and day-care procedures, it can be a practical choice for patients who need a defined operation and a short stay. The Chirag Enclave centre is close to Nehru Place and Greater Kailash hotels, while Karol Bagh has a Metro station nearby.",
	'batra-hospital-medical-research-centre':
		"##history\nBatra Hospital & Medical Research Centre was established in 1987 by the Ch. Aishi Ram Batra Public Charitable Trust as the first private multispeciality hospital in Delhi, with a vision of delivering quality healthcare at affordable prices. It was inaugurated by then Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi. It set up some of the earliest private-sector centres of excellence in Delhi in oncology, cardiology and nephrology, and has received recognition for patient safety, quality care and community health outreach.\n##specialities\nToday the hospital offers tertiary care in more than 40 specialities. Its centres of excellence include a heart centre, cancer centre, neurosciences centre, ortho and joint replacement centre, gastro sciences centre, dialysis and kidney transplant centre, and a urology department. It brings advanced care to life-threatening conditions in cardiac science, cancer, orthopaedics, nephrology and neurosurgery.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 500 beds, 14 operating theatres and around 110 ICU beds, along with round-the-clock emergency services, advanced diagnostic laboratories and comprehensive rehabilitation facilities. It is located on Mehrauli–Badarpur Road in the Tughlakabad Institutional Area, near Saket.\n##international\nBatra Hospital offers exclusive services for international patients, including visa assistance and pre-departure and post-departure support. Its medical experts have international experience.",
	'amrita-institute-of-medical-sciences-kochi':
		"##history\nAmrita Hospital in Ponekkara, Kochi, formerly the Amrita Institute of Medical Sciences (AIMS), was founded on 17 May 1998 by Mata Amritanandamayi Devi (Amma) as a multi-specialty tertiary referral and teaching hospital. It was awarded the FICCI National Healthcare Excellence Award for the best hospital in the country in 2013 and two further FICCI awards in 2016 for patient safety and innovation in medical technology. It is accredited by NABH, with laboratories accredited by NABL.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has 29 speciality departments and 17 centres of excellence, supported by about 670 faculty members and 4,000 support staff, and serves more than a million outpatients and over 70,000 inpatients annually. Milestones include Kerala's first simultaneous pancreas-kidney transplant (2014), South Asia's first bilateral hand transplant (2015) and, in 2021, the first double upper-limb transplant using HEMO2life graft preservation technology, its ninth such surgery. Services range from transfusion medicine and urology to craniomaxillofacial surgery and dermatology and cosmetology.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 1,100 to 1,450 beds according to different sources, making it one of the largest in South India. It sits in a large campus in Ponekkara, Kochi.\n##international\nAmrita has a dedicated team coordinating international patient treatment, with support for medical visas and accommodation, pre-visit medical opinions on treatment and costs, and multilingual interpretation.",
	'aster-medcity':
		"##history\nAster Medcity in Cheranalloor, Kochi, was established by Aster DM Healthcare in 2013 and began functioning as a soft launch in 2014. It sits on a 40-acre campus on the banks of the Kochi backwaters and is one of South Asia's largest quaternary-care healthcare centres. It was the first JCI-accredited quaternary-care multispecialty hospital in Kerala, and within its first year it also earned NABH accreditation, NABH nursing excellence certification and Green OT certification.\n##specialities\nAster Medcity is a multispecialty hospital with eight centres of excellence, including neurosciences, cardiac sciences, orthopaedics, oncology, gastroenterology, nephrology, urology, women's health, paediatrics, neonatology and multi-organ transplantation. A multidisciplinary transplant team of hepatologists, nephrologists, transplant surgeons and intensivists handles kidney, liver, heart and combined transplants. It is reported to be the first hospital in Kerala to offer Minimal Access Robotic Surgery with the da Vinci system, with more than 5,000 robotic-assisted surgeries reported across transplant, urology and gynaecology.\n##technology\nThe hospital is a large quaternary-care facility with several hundred beds; sources cite between about 670 and 800. Its campus was designed for patient comfort, with green certification.\n##international\nAster Medcity is a well-known destination for medical travellers in South India. Cheranalloor is close to Kochi city and about 25 to 30 km from Cochin International Airport.",
	'lakeshore-hospital':
		"##history\nVPS Lakeshore Hospital in Nettoor, Kochi, on the NH-66 bypass, is a multi super-speciality hospital that began functioning as a multi-specialty hospital in January 2003. It is NABH accredited and has been described as a premier destination for medical tourism. It received the Best Hospital for Medical Tourism award from the Government of Kerala in 2014, the Best Hospital in Kerala award from Worldwide Achievers in 2016 and Best Hospital in Oncology Services from the Times of India in 2017.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has more than 30 clinical departments, including multi-organ transplantation, gastroenterology, joint replacement, cardiology, cardiovascular surgery and neurology. Its nephrology and renal transplantation department has performed more than 1,600 transplants, and its cardiac sciences centre includes heart transplantation and ECMO. Milestones include Kerala's first liver transplant, the first paediatric bone marrow transplant, the state's first robotic knee replacement system and the first air, water and surface ambulance service in Kerala, recognised by the Limca Book of Records.\n##technology\nThe hospital has several hundred beds, with sources quoting about 470 to 650, and is a leader in organ transplantation, cardiac care and minimally invasive surgery.\n##international\nThe hospital offers 24-hour guest relations, advance payment options for international patients, customised cuisine, multilingual staff and acceptance of foreign currency.",
	'kims-health-kochi':
		"##history\nKIMS Health, Kochi, is the Kochi hospital of the KIMS group of institutions based in Thiruvananthapuram, which also has hospitals in the Middle East. Its hospital and surgical centre is located at Pathadipalam, Changampuzha Nagar Post, Edappally, and aims to provide world-class healthcare at affordable costs. It is accredited by NABH and by the Australian Council on Healthcare Standards International (ACHSI).\n##specialities\nThe hospital is a 125-bed multispecialty hospital with about 25 departments covering different ailments and diseases. It provides outpatient and inpatient departments, laboratory, pharmacy, X-ray, ECG and 24-hour services, supported by experienced consultants, trained nurses and paramedical staff.\n##technology\nThe hospital is modern and well equipped for a hospital of its size. Compared with the largest Kochi hospitals, it is a smaller facility, so patients with highly complex needs such as multi-organ transplants may be better served elsewhere.\n##international\nEdappally is a busy neighbourhood of Kochi close to Lulu Mall and Edappally railway station. Its convenient location and moderate size make it suitable for patients needing general or planned procedures in a comfortable setting.",
	'apollo-multispeciality-hospitals-kolkata':
		"##history\nApollo Multispeciality Hospitals, formerly Apollo Gleneagles, on Canal Circular Road in Kolkata, was established in 2003 and is a 700 to 750-bed tertiary-care hospital. It is the only hospital in Eastern India accredited by JCI. It has been named the No. 1 private hospital in Eastern and North Eastern India by The Week–Hansa Research survey for 12 consecutive years, and won the Global Health and Travel Awards' Best Multispecialty Hospital in Eastern India in 2019.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has more than 50 specialities and 33 centres of excellence, including heart care, cancer care, orthopaedics, gastroenterology, neurosciences, transplants, robotics and emergency care. It carried out Eastern India's first simultaneous heart, liver and kidney transplant and has brought complete robotic renal transplant to the region, and the Apollo group has performed more than 10,000 kidney transplants. It is also a trusted name for bone marrow transplants for international patients.\n##technology\nThe hospital handles more than 1,600 outpatient visits daily and has transplant centres equipped for living-donor and cadaver surgery.\n##international\nOver 10,000 international patients a year, many from Bangladesh, receive treatment at Apollo Kolkata, which has a dedicated international patient services team. It is in the Kankurgachi area of Kolkata.",
	'amri-hospitals-dhakuria':
		"##history\nAMRI Hospitals, Dhakuria, began in 1996 as a public-private venture with the Government of West Bengal, first as an outpatient facility, growing to a 150-bed hospital in 1997 and later expanding to a hospital of several hundred beds. Manipal Hospitals acquired a majority stake in the AMRI group in 2023, and the Dhakuria hospital is now Manipal Hospital Dhakuria (formerly AMRI), with Manipal present at Salt Lake, Dhakuria, Mukundapur and Broadway in Kolkata. Under the AMRI brand it was named Best Private Hospital in Eastern India at the ABP News Healthcare Leadership Awards in 2020 and 2021.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is known for cardiac sciences, joint replacement, trauma care, IVF, maxillofacial surgery and aesthetic and plastic surgery. Its emergency and critical care services are a centre of excellence. In 2024 it received awards at the Economic Times Healthcare Awards for contribution to emergency care and excellence in neurology and stroke management, and it was acknowledged by the Government of Bangladesh for its service to Bangladeshi patients.\n##technology\nAdvanced nuclear imaging includes PET-CT and SPECT-CT, and radiotherapy includes IMRT and VMAT. The hospital is accredited by NABH. It is at Gariahat Road, Dhakuria, in South Kolkata.\n##international\nManipal Hospitals offers dedicated services for international patients, including medical opinions, treatment planning, travel assistance and personalised support.",
	'fortis-hospital-anandapur':
		"##history\nFortis Hospital, Anandapur, in Kolkata was founded in 2011 and spans about seven acres on the Eastern Metropolitan Bypass. It is a 10-storey, roughly 300-bed establishment, with about 240 beds in operation. Milestones include the first custom-made knee replacement in Eastern India (2011), the first awake brain craniotomy in Eastern India (2012), India's first Heart Team launch (2012) and a paediatric renal transplant below 12 kg (2014). It received the Times Bengal Icons 2023 title for best trauma care medical facility in the city and awards at CAHOCON 2024.\n##specialities\nThe hospital specialises in cardiology and cardiac surgery, urology, nephrology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, digestive care, pulmonology, mother and child care, emergency services and critical care. It also has specialist clinics for pulmonary hypertension, non-invasive ventilation and allergies, and offers oncology, maxillofacial surgery, dentistry, psychiatry, diabetology, dermatology and ENT. Its cardiac centre has four cath labs, one cardiac OT, a 14-bed SICU and a 20-bed CCU.\n##technology\nThe hospital holds NABH accreditation and NABL certification.\n##international\nAs part of Fortis Healthcare, the hospital supports international patients through the group's international patient services. It is at Anandapur on the EM Bypass, well placed for the business districts and airport.",
	'medica-superspecialty-hospital':
		"##history\nMedica Superspecialty Hospital in Mukundapur was launched in 2010 and is part of the Medica group, described as the largest hospital chain in Eastern India. It is a tertiary-care hospital with several hundred beds, 18 departments and eight centres of excellence, at 127 Eastern Metropolitan Bypass. In February 2022 it installed the fourth-generation da Vinci robot, becoming the first official training centre for robotic surgery in Eastern India. It is also the first hospital in Eastern India with a certified Green Operation Theatre, and it received the Times Bengal Award in 2023.\n##specialities\nThe hospital covers anaesthesiology, cardiology, cardiac surgery, critical care, dermatology, dentistry, emergency medicine, endocrinology, ENT, gastroenterology, general and GI surgery, haematology, liver diseases, nephrology, neurology, neurosurgery, neurotology, nuclear medicine, orthopaedics, obstetrics and gynaecology, oncology, paediatric surgery, plastic and reconstructive surgery, rehabilitation, psychiatry, radiology, respiratory medicine, rheumatology, robotic surgery, transfusion medicine and urology.\n##technology\nMedica has one of the most advanced critical care units in the region, a NABL-accredited laboratory with a molecular lab and imaging services that meet international standards. Its dialysis centre was accredited in 2020 and it has won the best dialysis service provider award. The hospital is NABH and NABL accredited.\n##international\nMedica offers international patient services and is a well-known destination for patients from neighbouring countries.",
	'zydus-hospitals':
		"##history\nZydus Hospitals in Ahmedabad is an initiative of the Zydus Group and opened in 2015 on the S. G. Highway near Sola Bridge. It is a 550-bed super-speciality hospital across 16 floors and two basement floors, accredited by NABH and NABL. It was recognised as Best Hospital in Ahmedabad by The Week–Marg survey for four years and was Gujarat's 18th hospital to win the Global Green-OT award. The hospital has appointed American- and European-trained medical specialists.\n##specialities\nZydus is a hub for neurology, gastrointestinal care, urology, gynaecology, oncology, spine, cosmetic and plastic surgery, nephrology and ENT, with centres of excellence in IVF, joint replacement, cancer care, neurology, cardiac surgery, kidney transplant, liver transplant, neurosurgery and plastic surgery. Its liver transplant programme is supported by a multidisciplinary team of more than 20 specialists, and across its centres in Ahmedabad and Vadodara it has performed 430+ kidney transplants, 295+ liver transplants and 220+ bone marrow transplants.\n##technology\nThe hospital combines modern operating theatres, advanced imaging and large critical care capacity with green building practices.\n##international\nAhmedabad has emerged as a key destination in Western India, and Zydus attracts a growing share of international patients; its doctors also run health camps in African countries and Uzbekistan.",
	'cims-hospital':
		"##history\nCIMS Hospital, now Marengo Asia CIMS Hospital, opened in 2010 off Science City Road in Sola, Ahmedabad, and is part of the Marengo Asia Hospitals group. It is a multi-super speciality green hospital accredited by NABH, NABL and JCI. In October 2023 its team, led by Dr. Dhiren Shah, performed what it reports as Asia's first bloodless heart transplant, using a goal-directed bleeding management protocol; the patient was discharged in nine days compared with the usual 21 to 24 days.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers cancer care, cardiac sciences, gastroenterology, liver transplant and biliary sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, neurosciences, bone marrow transplant, bariatric surgery, clinical psychology, rheumatology, diabetic foot, dental and dermatology. Dr. Dhiren Shah, director of the heart transplant programme and Gujarat's first heart transplant surgeon, has more than 16,000 CABG surgeries and about 50 heart transplants to his name, and was the first in India to perform trans-aortic TAVR and hybrid CABG. The hospital has a dedicated transplant centre for heart, liver, kidney, lung and paediatric bone marrow transplants.\n##technology\nThe hospital is described as a 300 to 500 bed facility, opposite Shukan Mall, with advanced ICUs and operating theatres.\n##international\nThe hospital treats patients from India and abroad.",
	'sterling-hospital':
		"##history\nSterling Hospitals in Gurukul, Memnagar, Ahmedabad, was established in 2001 as a tertiary-care hospital and has grown into a network of hospitals across Gujarat. In 2009 it became the first hospital in Gujarat to be fully accredited by NABH, and its laboratories were the first in Gujarat to be accredited by NABL. It was named Best Hospital for three consecutive years (2007 to 2009) by IMRB and The Week.\n##specialities\nSterling provides cardiac sciences, oncology (surgical, medical and radiation), critical care and pulmonology, gastroenterology and GI surgery, neurosciences and spine surgery, nephrology and urology, orthopaedics and joint replacement, obstetrics and gynaecology, haematology, trauma care, bariatric surgery, ENT and anaesthesiology. It performed the first liver transplant in the region, introduced CRRT dialysis, and set up Gujarat's first bone marrow unit and the state's largest dialysis facility. It is recognised as a leading cardiac centre in Ahmedabad.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 300 beds. Its paediatric and neonatal ICUs are equipped with multi-parameter monitoring, ventilators and ECMO and a high nurse-to-patient ratio.\n##international\nSterling reports treating more than 20,000 international patients a year from over 130 countries, through a one-stop international patient service that coordinates the hospital, doctors and patients.",
	'shalby-hospitals':
		"##history\nShalby Hospitals began in Ahmedabad in 1994 as a joint replacement centre started by Dr. Vikram I. Shah, and over about 30 years has become one of India's fastest-growing multi-specialty tertiary hospital chains across western, central and northern India. The Ahmedabad flagship, Shalby Multispeciality Hospital, is on S. G. Highway near Ramdev Nagar, Satellite, and was founded in 2007. Dr. Shah has been chairman of Shalby and chief of its joint replacement programme since 1993, and received the Dr. B. C. Roy International Award in 2003. In 2025 the group received the Hurun India Healthcare Transformation and Medical Excellence Award and an award for best hospital for medical tourism in Gujarat.\n##specialities\nShalby is renowned worldwide for joint replacement, with more than 150,000 replacements performed. Dr. Shah and his team perform more than 800 primary joint replacements a month, and his ZERO technique has cut the surgical time of a knee replacement from about 80 minutes to about 10 to 12 minutes. The group has also received the Rajiv Gandhi National Quality Award and FICCI awards.\n##technology\nThe SG Highway hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL, with about 200 beds.\n##international\nShalby has a special international patient desk offering video consultations, travel and visa assistance, accommodation help and free airport pickup and drop-off.",
	'dr-agarwal-s-eye-hospital':
		"##history\nDr. Agarwal's Eye Hospital was founded in 1957 in Chennai by Padma Bhushan Dr. Jaiveer Agarwal and Dr. Tahira Agarwal. Dr. Jaiveer Agarwal received the Padma Bhushan in March 2006. Over the decades it has grown into one of India's largest eye-care chains, with centres in 14 states and four union territories and in several countries overseas, especially in Africa. The exact number of centres varies by source and changes over time, so patients should check the current list of Delhi-NCR locations when planning.\n##specialities\nThe hospital provides comprehensive ophthalmology, including cataract surgery using techniques such as phacoemulsification and femtosecond laser assistance, LASIK and other refractive surgery, retina care for conditions such as diabetic retinopathy and retinal detachment, glaucoma, cornea and paediatric ophthalmology. The group is also associated with well-known ophthalmic surgeons and researchers, including Dr. Amar Agarwal, noted for innovations in cataract surgery.\n##technology\nMost eye procedures are done as day care, which makes it practical for international visitors. Delhi-NCR has several Dr. Agarwal's centres.\n##international\nBecause many eye procedures require only a short stay, patients can often combine treatment with travel in the region.",
	'aakash-healthcare-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nAakash Healthcare Super Speciality Hospital was founded in 2011 in Sector 3, Dwarka, and has grown into a 230-bed tertiary-care hospital serving West Delhi and the wider NCR. It has been recognised by The Week magazine as one of Delhi's youngest multispeciality hospitals for its rapid growth, and has received healthcare excellence recognition in the Economic Times Healthcare Awards 2021 and an India's Most Trusted Healthcare award in 2023.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is best known for orthopaedics and joint replacement, and also runs centres of excellence in cardiology, general and minimal access surgery, ophthalmology and refractive error surgery, mother and child care, neurology and neurosurgery, and renal sciences. Departments span anaesthesiology, clinical immunology and rheumatology, dentistry, dermatology, ENT, gastroenterology, haematology, hepatology, internal medicine, laparoscopic surgery, nephrology, oncology, pain management, pulmonology, radiology and urology, and it supports liver and kidney transplant care.\n##technology\nWith 70 critical care beds and 15 dialysis stations, the hospital is equipped for complex cases. It uses robotic surgery, a 3T MRI and a 128-slice CT scanner, and has modern ICUs and 24/7 emergency services. It is accredited by NABH and NABL, is empanelled with CGHS, and holds ISO certification.\n##international\nAakash Healthcare provides services for international patients, including visa assistance, flight bookings, accommodation arrangements and airport transfers, with a dedicated team offering personalised assistance. Located in Dwarka, close to the Metro network and the international airport, it is a convenient base for patients needing joint replacement, cardiac or neurological care.",
	'manipal-hospital-dwarka':
		"##history\nManipal Hospital Dwarka is part of the Manipal Hospitals network, one of India's largest healthcare groups, and serves West Delhi as a multi-super speciality tertiary-care hospital. The group has been recognised with many awards, and the Dwarka hospital has been honoured for patient safety, emergency and critical care, gastroenterology and orthopaedics, according to hospital and directory listings.\n##specialities\nThe hospital houses centres of excellence in orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences (nephrology and urology), cardiac sciences, medical and surgical gastroenterology, neurosciences and oncology, plus obstetrics and gynaecology and paediatrics. It also has dedicated programmes for liver transplantation and cancer care. More than 120 doctors with experience in complex and advanced cases work at the hospital.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 13 modular operation theatres and 118 critical care beds, with a 24/7 emergency and trauma department staffed by critical care specialists. It integrates AI-enabled diagnostics, telemedicine, robotic surgery, O-arm imaging, electronic medical records and a pneumatic chute system. It is accredited by NABH and NABL.\n##international\nManipal Hospital Dwarka offers international patient services. Its location in Sector 6, Dwarka, is close to Dwarka Metro stations and about a short drive from Indira Gandhi International Airport, making arrival and outpatient visits straightforward.",
	'sir-ganga-ram-hospital':
		"##history\nSir Ganga Ram Hospital in Rajinder Nagar owes its origin to Sir Ganga Ram, a renowned engineer and philanthropist, and has been delivering care since 1954. Over the decades it has recorded several firsts in India: the country's first successful liver transplant in 1989, the first Centre for Chest Surgery in 1991, the first Bloodless Medicine and Surgery Centre in 2001, and North India's first comprehensive robotic surgery centre in 2012. The hospital notes that 21 Padma award winners have come from its hospitals.\n##specialities\nKey departments include cardiology and the Dharma Vira Heart Centre, oncology, gastroenterology, orthopaedics, neurology and obstetrics, alongside genetic medicine, minimal access and bariatric surgery, surgical gastroenterology, sleep medicine, endocrinology and metabolism, nuclear medicine, a day-care centre, homoeopathy, Ayurveda, liver transplantation, cochlear implants and physiotherapy. The hospital operates one of the country's most prolific liver transplant programmes, and more than 70% of liver transplants in the country are done by surgeons who are alumni of this department.\n##technology\nThe hospital has around 675 beds, including ICU and private wards, and is accredited by NABH and NABL with ISO-certified quality systems. Its nephrology department began in 1981, the first kidney transplant was performed in 1987, and almost 6,000 kidneys have been transplanted since, with about 250 transplants each year.\n##international\nSir Ganga Ram Hospital is nationally recognised for its kidney and liver transplant programme, with outcomes comparable to international standards through a multidisciplinary team. It is located on Pusa Road in Rajinder Nagar, close to Rajendra Place and Karol Bagh.",
	'amrita-hospital':
		"##history\nAmrita Hospital's Faridabad campus was inaugurated in August 2022 by Prime Minister Narendra Modi. The hospital was founded on the vision of Sri Mata Amritanandamayi Devi (Amma), is owned and managed by the Mata Amritanandamayi Math, and operates as a non-profit-oriented institution. It is described as the largest private multi-specialty hospital in Asia, spread over 130 acres with about 3.6 million square feet of built-up area.\n##specialities\nWith a planned capacity of 2,600 beds and more than 80 specialities, the hospital has eight centres of excellence: cancer care, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, digestive diseases, orthopaedics and joint replacement, renal sciences, solid-organ transplantation, and mother and child care. It is home to South Asia's first successful bilateral hand transplant and performed India's first fully robotic donor hepatectomy, with over 350 robotic donor liver operations reported.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 534 critical care beds monitored by AI-enabled systems, advanced imaging including a Discovery PET-CT, 3 Tesla MRI and a dual-head SPECT-CT, and a strong programme in robotic surgery. It holds NABH, NABL and AACI accreditation, and received the FICCI Healthcare Excellence Award 2025 for patient safety.\n##international\nAmrita Hospital has a dedicated International Patient Division, designed to serve patients from over 50 countries with cultural sensitivity and multilingual support, including interpreters in Arabic, Russian, French and Swahili. Faridabad is about an hour from central Delhi and the airport.",
	'metro-heart-institute-with-multispeciality':
		"##history\nMetro Heart Institute with Multispeciality in Faridabad has operated since 2002 as the first dedicated heart hospital in Haryana, part of the Metro group of hospitals set up in 1997 by Dr. Purshotam Lal. Dr. Lal, known as the father of interventional cardiology in India, received the Padma Bhushan in 2003, the Padma Vibhushan in 2009 and the Dr. B. C. Roy National Award. He is credited with the first ASD closure without surgery in 1992 and the first non-surgical aortic valve replacement with a CoreValve in 2004.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers cardiac services including angioplasty, pacemaker implantation and heart surgery, supported by dedicated cardiac ICUs. Its cardiac team has performed over 75,000 angiographies and angioplasties and over 10,000 cardiac surgeries. Milestones include the first TAVI in Faridabad, the region's first combined heart and brain surgery and the first minimally invasive heart surgery in Faridabad. It has grown to over 30 specialities, including kidney transplants, mammography for early cancer detection and a large bone marrow transplant unit.\n##technology\nThe hospital has more than 400 beds, over 200 experts and more than 1,000 staff, and holds NABH, NABL and KVQA accreditation.\n##international\nMetro Heart Institute combines evidence-based treatment and internationally trained doctors to care for both Indian and international patients. It is located in Sector 16A, Faridabad, on the Delhi–Faridabad corridor with Metro access.",
	'the-sight-avenue':
		"##history\nThe Sight Avenue is a super-speciality eye hospital founded by Dr. Suraj Munjal, who has nearly two decades of experience and serves as founder and chief surgeon. He has completed more than 25,000 cataract surgeries, 10,000 LASIK procedures, 1,000 squint surgeries and 1,000 corneal transplants, received the Best Paper Award at AIOS 2008 for work in squint surgery, and has been a faculty member for the Delhi Ophthalmological Society for several consecutive years. He is reported to own the country's first robotic cataract system.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers bladeless laser cataract surgery, LASIK, Femto robotic LASIK, small-flap blade-free vision correction, SMILE, implantable collamer lenses, Contoura Vision, squint surgery, glaucoma care, dry-eye treatment, oculoplasty, cornea and keratoconus care, retina and uvea services, diabetic retinopathy treatment, ocular oncology and paediatric ophthalmology. It was among the first in Gurugram to introduce Contoura Vision LASIK and has completed over 1,000 SMILE surgeries.\n##technology\nThe hospital uses femtosecond laser technology for painless cataract surgery and offers multifocal and toric lenses. It has treated over 50,000 patients across its centres.\n##international\nThe Sight Avenue has centres in Greater Kailash, New Delhi (Hansraj Gupta Road) and in Sector 38, Gurugram, near Bakhtawar Chowk. Both are convenient for visitors staying in South Delhi or Gurugram hotels, and vision-correction procedures are typically short, making it practical to combine treatment with travel.",
	'shroff-eye-centre':
		"##history\nShroff Eye Centre is one of India's oldest and most trusted eye centres, with a legacy of more than 100 years and four generations of eye care. Dr. Noshir Shroff was awarded the Padma Bhushan in 2010 and is known for pioneering intraocular lens implantation in India. The Delhi centre has been operating in Kailash Colony since 1973, and Dr. Cyrus Shroff joined the team in 1984.\n##specialities\nThe centre offers phacoemulsification (stitchless) cataract surgery with monofocal, multifocal and toric intraocular lenses, and refractive surgery including LASIK, Femto Contoura, SILK, ICL, PRK and Streamlight. Its surgical retina team performs vitreo-retinal surgery for diabetic retinopathy, macular holes and retinal detachment, and it provides cornea treatment, glaucoma management, paediatric ophthalmology and uveitis and neuro-ophthalmology expertise. It runs one of Delhi NCR's few dedicated dry-eye clinics, using Lipiview and Lipiflow technology and IPL.\n##technology\nThe centre holds NABH accreditation and is consistently ranked among the top eye hospitals in NCR and North India in health surveys. With four centres across Delhi NCR, it has a team of more than 40 specialists and about 125 staff, handling more than 100,000 patient visits and over 10,000 eye surgeries each year.\n##international\nShroff Eye Centre has centres in Kailash Colony and Connaught Place, both easy to reach by Metro. For international patients, the centre offers a full range of vision-correction and eye-surgery options in one place.",
	'eye7-hospitals':
		"##history\nEye7 Eye Hospitals, formerly Chaudhary Eye Centre, has a legacy of more than two decades and was established under the leadership of ophthalmologist Dr. Sanjay Chaudhary. It has performed over 200,000 surgeries across its centres and pioneered Contoura Vision for spectacle removal in India. Today it is led by Managing Director Dr. Rahil Chaudhary, who holds a Guinness World Record for 250 LASIK surgeries in a single day, a Limca Book of Records entry for correcting -32.5 D with ICL, and an India Book of Records entry for the fastest LASIK in India.\n##specialities\nServices include Contoura Vision, LASIK, ICL, refractive lens exchange, cataract, glaucoma, retina, cornea, squint, neuro-ophthalmology, oculoplasty, paediatric ophthalmology and low vision. Dr. Rahil Chaudhary has received awards including the Young ICL Ophthalmologist award, the International Hero in Ophthalmology award from the All India Ophthalmological Society, and the Best Surgical Technique and John Henahan prizes at the ESCRS.\n##technology\nEye7 offers a Contoura Vision refractive suite, the femtosecond FS 200 and EX500 lasers for bladeless LASIK and the EVO Implantable Collamer Lens from STAAR Surgical. The hospitals are NABH accredited and are on the panels of CGHS, MCD, ECHS and the Directorate of Health Services.\n##international\nEye7 operates several centres across Delhi, including Lajpat Nagar and Janakpuri, all well connected to central and South Delhi. Because vision-correction procedures are usually day-care, patients can often plan a short stay.",
	'sharp-sight-eye-hospitals':
		"##history\nSharp Sight Eye Hospitals is a chain of eye-care centres based in Delhi that has expanded across North India and opened new centres in cities such as Prayagraj, Patna, Jhansi and Asansol. It has received recognition including Best Eye Care Provider from the Times of India, Best Outreach Program in Ophthalmology from Business World, and medical tourism and healthcare awards in 2020. It was among the first eye hospitals in Delhi to be accredited by NABH.\n##specialities\nSharp Sight offers cataract surgery by conventional and advanced laser techniques, bladeless painless LASIK, glaucoma care, squint and lazy-eye treatment, diabetic retinopathy care, cornea services and paediatric ophthalmology. Its cataract surgery is completed in about 15 minutes, and its retinal surgeons rely on diagnostic tools such as FFA, B-scan ultrasound and OCT. It was among the first in Delhi to introduce femto cataract surgery.\n##technology\nThe hospitals are equipped with advanced diagnostic tools, NABH accredited and endorsed by CGHS. The chain reports around 40,000 patient visits and over 3,500 ophthalmic surgeries annually at its network.\n##international\nThe Delhi hospital near Preet Vihar Metro on Vikas Marg in East Delhi is convenient for visitors staying in the Anand Vihar and Preet Vihar areas.",
	'venu-eye-institute-research-centre':
		"##history\nVenu Eye Institute & Research Centre was established in 1986 under the Venu Charitable Society by the late Dr. R. K. Seth, an eminent ophthalmologist who wanted to reach patients beyond the limits of private practice. Venu pioneered a three-tier service delivery network to bring quality eye care to people in rural and underserved areas. Today it is led by Managing Director Ms. Tanuja Joshi, and continues to focus on emerging challenges such as glaucoma, diabetic retinopathy and macular degeneration.\n##specialities\nThe institute provides ophthalmic outpatient and inpatient care to paying and subsidised patients under one roof. Services include eye surgery, LASIK, refractive surgery, cornea, glaucoma and retina treatment, oculoplasty, squint surgery, orbital tumour surgery and contact lens services, together with affordable treatment and training for healthcare professionals.\n##technology\nThe hospital is located on a 2.5-acre plot in Sheikh Sarai Phase II in South Delhi, is empanelled under CGHS, and has served millions of patients over more than four decades, a large share of them free of cost or at subsidised rates.\n##international\nVenu is a good choice for patients looking for a well-established, mission-driven eye hospital with a full range of services in South Delhi. It is open Monday to Saturday, 8:30 am to 5:00 pm.",
	'guru-nanak-eye-centre':
		"##history\nGuru Nanak Eye Centre (GNEC) was conceived in 1971 to upgrade the ophthalmology department into a full-fledged institution and is attached to Maulana Azad Medical College. Its outpatient block became operational in 1977, while indoor wards and operation theatres continued to run in Irwin Hospital until a 184-bed ward block and operating facilities were added to the campus in 1993. It is run by the Government of Delhi and is located on Maharaja Ranjit Singh Marg, near the Ram Lila Grounds and New Delhi Railway Station.\n##specialities\nThe centre has six ophthalmic units, with two units posted together in the outpatient department, wards and operation theatre. Its super-speciality clinics include cornea, retina, glaucoma, contact lens services, neuro-ophthalmology for optic nerve and central nervous system disorders, paediatric ophthalmology, and squint and strabismus. Clinics run on scheduled days of the week, and a well-supported investigative laboratory and pharmacy complete the service.\n##technology\nAll outpatient services are provided free of cost, with 24 to 28 ophthalmologists available in the outpatient department every day. GNEC is a teaching and training institution offering ophthalmology residency programmes, and its faculty and residents have won a notable share of All India Ophthalmological Society awards.\n##international\nAs a government teaching institute, GNEC is best suited to patients who need a public-sector academic centre with broad ophthalmic expertise. Because procedures and queues follow government rules, it is worth confirming timings and waiting lists in advance and comparing with private options.",
	'shining-smile-dentistry':
		"##history\nShining Smiles Dentistry is a dental clinic in Saket, New Delhi, established in 2021 and led by two dentists, Dr. Shashank Arora and Dr. Anika Bhasin Arora. The clinic is located in the basement at F-36, Press Enclave Marg, opposite Gate 5 of the Max hospital complex, close to the Saket district centre. It has quickly become known for dental implants, immediate implants and smile makeovers.\n##specialities\nDr. Shashank Arora holds a BDS and an MDS, has more than 15 years of experience as an endodontist and implantologist, and performs procedures under a microscope. He holds a diploma in immediate functional loading implants, has 14 research publications and has presented internationally. Dr. Anika Bhasin Arora holds a BDS and an MDS in endodontics, and has more than 12 years of experience in cosmetic dentistry and root canal treatment. The clinic offers dental implants, Hollywood smile design, veneers, Invisalign, crowns, sinus lift, bone grafting, root canal treatment, teeth cleaning and digital smile design.\n##technology\nTreatment rooms are equipped with digital X-rays, 3D scanners and intraoral cameras for precise diagnosis and planning. Microscopic dentistry allows root canal treatment and other procedures to be carried out with high accuracy.\n##international\nSmile design and implant treatment often require a few visits spread over several days, which suits patients combining dental work with a trip to Delhi. Saket has Metro connections, hotels and shopping close by.",
	'spruce-dental-chain-of-clinics':
		"##history\nSpruce Dental Chain of Clinics is led by Dr. Javed Rizwan, director and head of the group, and operates a clinic behind Medanta Hospital in Sector 38, Gurugram, also known as Smile Garden Dental Implant Center. Dr. Rizwan holds a BDS and an MDS in dentofacial orthopaedics and has a Master's in strategic implantology from Germany, where he trained under a pioneer of corticobasal implantology in Munich. He has more than 20 years of experience.\n##specialities\nThe clinic is known for root canal treatment, immediate implants, conventional implants and smile design, together with cosmetic dentistry, braces and aligners, laser gum treatment and jaw surgeries. Dr. Rizwan has placed more than 15,000 dental implants, including conventional and immediate implants, and more than 500 full-mouth cases using immediate strategic implants. Implants are made of titanium or zirconia and are placed in the jawbone to replace missing teeth.\n##technology\nSpruce Dental is an ISO 9001:2015 certified group, and it runs clinical residency programmes in general dentistry and implantology at its Mahendru Enclave clinic in Delhi. The Gurugram clinic works Monday to Saturday and offers emergency support.\n##international\nThe clinic is next to Medanta Hospital, which makes it easy to reach for international visitors staying in Gurugram, and full-mouth implant treatment can often be planned around a short stay.",
	'asg-eye-hospital':
		"##history\nASG Eye Hospital was founded in Jodhpur, Rajasthan, in December 2005 by AIIMS alumni Dr. Arun Singhvi and Dr. Shilpi Gang. It has grown from a single hospital into one of India's largest eye-care networks, with more than 150 hospitals in over 80 cities in India and hospitals in Uganda and Nepal, and reports serving millions of patients. Its founders have received recognition including the All India Achievers Award and youth entrepreneur awards, and Dr. Singhvi received the ISCKRS Young Entrepreneur Award in 2022.\n##specialities\nASG treats cataract, LASIK, glaucoma, retinal diseases, oculoplasty, corneal problems, squint, paediatric ophthalmology and neuro-ophthalmology. Its cataract surgery uses premium intraocular lenses for faster recovery, LASIK includes Contoura and PRK, and retina services cover diabetic retinopathy treatment and vitreo-retinal surgery.\n##technology\nThe network is known for femtosecond lasers for cataract surgery, LASIK lasers, advanced vitreo-retinal surgery, squint and oculoplastic surgery, cosmetic eye surgery, an approved eye bank and 24-hour emergency services for eye trauma. The Noida hospital is at V-21A, Atta Market, Sector 27, and diagnoses and treats complex eye diseases under one roof.\n##international\nNoida is well connected to Delhi by Metro and expressway, and eye procedures are typically short, day-care treatments.",
	'eye-q-super-speciality-eye-hospitals':
		"##history\nEye-Q Super-Speciality Eye Hospitals started in 2007 with the aim of providing eye care to everyone, including common people, at affordable cost and at the level of tier II, III and IV cities. Its founder and CMD, Dr. Ajay Sharma, completed his MBBS at PGIMS Rohtak and did fellowships in cataract microsurgery at the L V Prasad Eye Institute, and was among the first surgeons in India to introduce phacoemulsification in 1996. He has received gold medals and awards, and the group was named Best Eye Care Service Provider by Frost & Sullivan in 2012. Eye-Q now has more than 30 hospitals across Haryana, Uttar Pradesh, Uttarakhand and Gujarat and hospitals in Nigeria, and reports treating over 7.5 million patients.\n##specialities\nEye-Q provides LASIK, cataract, retina, oculoplasty, glaucoma, neuro-ophthalmology, squint, opticals and pharmacy services. Its cataract surgery is laser-automated, bladeless and painless, and retinal tears and detachments are treated with surgery combined with laser photocoagulation and cryopexy.\n##technology\nGurugram has several centres, including Sector 27 on Golf Course Road (Plot 531, DLF Phase IV), Sector 46, New Railway Road and DLF Cyber City. Patients benefit from experienced surgeons, advanced technology and consistent outcomes.\n##international\nThe Golf Course Road centre is close to Gurugram hotels and the Cyber City business district.",
	'medanta-the-medicity':
		"##history\nMedanta – The Medicity was founded by the renowned cardiac surgeon Dr. Naresh Trehan and began operating in 2009 on a 43-acre campus in Sector 38, Gurugram. It is one of India's largest multi-super speciality hospitals and has been ranked India's number one hospital in Newsweek's World's Best Hospitals for seven consecutive years (2020–2026). Milestones include India's first successful intestinal transplant in 2013, Asia's first bloodless bone marrow transplant, India's first air ambulance service (Flying Doctors India, 2013) and a world record of 30 total knee replacements in a single day.\n##specialities\nMedanta has 29 super-speciality units and more than 800 doctors, with six centres of excellence: cardiac sciences, neurosciences, bone and joint, cancer, renal and urology, and liver transplant. Its Heart Institute, led by Dr. Trehan, is one of Asia's largest cardiac centres, and it has performed more than 15,000 cardiac surgeries and 2,500 joint replacements. Its liver transplant programme, led by Dr. A. S. Soin, has performed over 500 living-donor liver transplants, the highest in India.\n##technology\nThe hospital uses robotic surgery with the da Vinci system, AI-based diagnostics and advanced radiotherapy, and was the first in India to start robotic surgery for cardiology, gynaecology and urology. It is accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL.\n##international\nMedanta treats around 20,000 international patients each year from more than 130 countries, offering visa support, airport transfers, interpreters and personalised care. It is about 18 km from the international airport.",
	'fortis-memorial-research-institute-fmri':
		"##history\nFortis Memorial Research Institute (FMRI) in Sector 44, Gurugram, was established in 2001 and is the flagship hospital of Fortis Healthcare. It is a multi-super speciality, quaternary-care hospital built on four pillars of talent, technology, infrastructure and service. It received the FICCI Medical Value Travel Award in 2019 for neurosciences, spine surgery and bone marrow transplant, and has featured in Newsweek's World's Best Smart Hospitals and Best Hospitals in India rankings.\n##specialities\nFMRI has centres of excellence in robotic surgery, oncology (medical, surgical, gynaecological and radiation), cardiology and cardiac surgery, kidney and liver transplants, haematology, haemato-oncology and bone marrow transplant, gastroenterology and GI surgery, neurology and neurosurgery, urology, orthopaedics, joint replacement and sports medicine, minimal-access and bariatric surgery and paediatrics. Its bone marrow transplant programme is among the largest in North India, with several thousand transplants reported across its history.\n##technology\nThe hospital is set on an 11-acre campus near HUDA City Centre Metro station. It is accredited by JCI, NABH, NABL and CEA, and combines advanced diagnostics, operating theatres and critical care with cutting-edge technology.\n##international\nFMRI provides dedicated international patient services, including treatment planning, medical opinions, visa assistance, airport pickup, language interpreters, accommodation support and post-treatment follow-up. Its location beside HUDA City Centre Metro makes it convenient for visitors.",
	'sanar-international-hospitals':
		"##history\nSanar International Hospitals, now Shalby Sanar International Hospital, was founded by Mr. Naresh Kapoor and opened around 2018 on Golf Course Road in Sector 53, Gurugram. It later became part of the Shalby group, founded by Dr. Vikram I. Shah, which began as a joint replacement centre in Ahmedabad and has performed more than 150,000 joint replacements. The hospital was the first in Gurugram to receive AACI accreditation and is also accredited by JCI and NABH. It is one of the first hospitals in India to receive Les Clefs d'Or concierge membership for luxury services to international patients.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is a multi-super speciality facility with more than 30 specialities and centres of excellence in oncology, neurosciences, nephrology, orthopaedics, gastroenterology, transplants and critical care. It offers cancer care, heart care, blood and marrow transplants, kidney and liver transplants, and is best known for bone and joint services. Its orthopaedic team has expertise in revision hip and knee replacement using computer navigation, special implants and frozen bone grafts.\n##technology\nThe hospital has around 150 beds, including about 35 ICU beds with transplant ICU capability, and is part of a group with thousands of doctors, surgeons and support staff.\n##international\nThe hospital is a preferred destination for medical travellers and has treated patients from countries including Iraq, Yemen, Uzbekistan, Kyrgyzstan, Russia, Kenya, Ghana, Somalia, Ethiopia, Bangladesh and Fiji. It provides dedicated international patient services, travel coordination, interpreters and customised treatment plans.",
	'jaypee-hospital':
		"##history\nJaypee Hospital in Sector 128, Noida, is the flagship healthcare initiative of the Jaypee Group, set on a 25-acre campus and among the NCR's leading multi-speciality hospitals. It has been recognised as Best Multi-Speciality Hospital in UP/NCR (Times Healthcare 2017–18), among the top critical care hospitals in North India (Times Health Survey 2017) and Emerging Health Brand of the Year (Radio City Awards 2016). The hospital was acquired by Max Healthcare in 2024 and now also operates as Max Super Speciality Hospital, Noida (Sector 128), so patients may see either name when booking.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers more than 30 super-specialities, including organ transplant, cancer care, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, orthopaedics, gastroenterology, nephrology, IVF and reproductive medicine, bariatric surgery, ENT and aesthetic and reconstructive surgery. Its Heart Institute has cardiac operating theatres, hybrid cath labs and a dedicated coronary ICU, and its Institute for Organ Transplant covers liver, kidney, heart, cornea and bone marrow transplants, with reports of more than 1,000 kidney and over 350 liver transplants.\n##technology\nWith 525+ operational beds, 150+ ICU beds, a 24-bed neonatal ICU, a 12-bed transplant ICU and 18 modular operation theatres with laminar airflow, the hospital is equipped for complex care. It offers the da Vinci robotic system for urology, gynaecology and general surgery, and is accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL.\n##international\nJaypee Hospital operates a dedicated international patient services desk that supports overseas patients with appointment scheduling, treatment package planning, pre-arrival teleconsultation, medical opinions, visa documentation guidance, airport pickup and customised diet plans.",
	'marengo-asia-hospitals':
		"##history\nMarengo Asia Hospitals in Sector 16, Faridabad, was formerly known as QRG Health City and is now part of the Marengo Asia Healthcare network, founded by Dr. Raajiv Singhal, which operates over 2,500 beds across eight multi-specialty hospitals. The Faridabad hospital is a modern, patient-friendly multi-super speciality hospital and has been serving the region since 2007. Recent milestones include the region's first robotic knee replacement in December 2025 and the first LVAD in Faridabad.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers oncology, cardiac sciences, gastroenterology, liver transplant and biliary sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, bone marrow transplant, renal sciences and neurosciences, along with a critical care medicine unit for patients with life-threatening conditions. Across the Marengo Asia group, notable achievements include Asia's first bloodless heart transplant in Ahmedabad and India's first psycho-neurosurgery for schizophrenia for a patient from Kenya in Gurugram.\n##technology\nThe hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL and has cutting-edge diagnostic and imaging technology, including MRI, CT scan and endoscopic ultrasound. It has several hundred beds and a dedicated critical care unit.\n##international\nMarengo Asia promotes international clinical collaborations, including partnerships with experts and health ministries of partner countries to establish centres of excellence. Faridabad is easily reached from Delhi by the Metro and expressway.",
	'marengo-asia-hospitals-gurugram':
		"##history\nMarengo Asia Hospitals in Sector 56, Gurugram, was formerly W Pratiksha Hospital and has been rebranded under the Marengo Asia Healthcare network. It is a multispecialty tertiary and quaternary care hospital of about 250 beds on Golf Course Extension Road, Sushant Lok II, with more than 150,000 square feet of built-up area in a calm setting. The hospital reports over 6,000 joint replacements and 5,500 successful IVF procedures.\n##specialities\nThe hospital covers more than 21 specialities, including cardiology, neurology, orthopaedics, urology, oncology, fertility, women's health and critical care. Its Marengo Asia International Institute of Neuro & Spine (MAIINS) is a centre of excellence, led by internationally renowned neurologist Dr. Praveen Gupta. MAIINS brings together neurologists, spine surgeons, psychiatrists, psychologists, pain specialists and rehabilitation experts to provide protocol-driven care for neurological and spine conditions.\n##technology\nThe institute is equipped with robotic-assisted spine surgery systems, advanced neuro-monitoring, dedicated neuro ICUs and integrated rehabilitation services. The hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL.\n##international\nThe hospital is positioned to serve international patients with modern infrastructure aligned to international standards; the wider Marengo network has treated patients from countries such as Kenya. It is on Golf Course Extension Road, close to Gurugram hotels and business districts.",
	'fortis-hospital':
		"##history\nFortis Hospital, Noida, in Sector 62 was established in 2004 and is the second-largest hub hospital in the Fortis group after Fortis Gurugram. It has become a leading multi-specialty tertiary-care hospital that has helped transform healthcare infrastructure in the NCR. It is designated a Heart Command Centre for Uttar Pradesh and is a high-volume transplant and trauma referral centre.\n##specialities\nThe hospital reports more than 15,000 knee replacements, 15,000 neurosurgeries, over 3,000 liver and kidney transplants and 10,000 cardiac procedures, including more than 750 liver transplants. Its cardiac programme covers ECMO, TAVI, LVAD, heart transplant and complex surgery supported by twin cath labs, and its neurosciences and orthopaedics departments use neuro-navigation and keyhole spine surgery, with dedicated neuro ICUs. It is also strong in oncology, gastroenterology and hepatobiliary sciences, urology and general surgery.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 200 beds with 12 operation theatres and advanced ICU facilities. It has been recognised with AHPI awards for infection control and nursing practices, the World Stroke Organization's diamond award for stroke management, and FICCI's medical value travel award for liver transplant (2023). It is NABH accredited.\n##international\nFortis Noida offers full international patient services, including visa assistance and language support, with international patient coordinators, specialised nursing teams and rehabilitation therapists. It is well connected to Delhi by the Metro and expressway.",
	'fortis-hospital-shalimar-bagh':
		"##history\nFortis Hospital, Shalimar Bagh, was established in 2010 and is a 262-bed multi-super speciality hospital on a 7.34-acre campus in North West Delhi. It is India's first hospital registered under the Green Building Rating System and holds a three-star rating from the Bureau of Energy Efficiency. It has received the National Quality Excellence Award (2018) and the AHPI Excellence in Nursing Practice Award (2024).\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers centres of excellence in critical care, emergency and trauma, neurosciences, bone and joint, cardiac sciences and gastro sciences, along with oncology, obstetrics and gynaecology, kidney transplant, nephrology, urology and neonatology with a Level III NICU. It is recognised for cardiac bypass surgery, interventional, non-invasive and paediatric cardiology and paediatric cardiac surgery, and is a certified centre of excellence for bariatric surgery. Its bariatric team addresses weight-related conditions such as type 2 diabetes, GERD and high blood pressure.\n##technology\nTechnology includes the da Vinci surgical robot, a Versa HD linear accelerator, a PET-CT scanner, the CORI robotic system for knee replacement and advanced neuro-navigation. The hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL, with NABH nursing excellence and ethics committee certification and Green OT certification.\n##international\nFacilities for international patients include private rooms, Wi-Fi, accessible rooms, lodging for families, laundry, concierge services and more. The hospital houses the Fortis Ridge IVF Centre. It is well connected to central Delhi by the Metro.",
	'fortis-hospital-faridabad':
		"##history\nFortis Escorts Hospital, Faridabad, on Neelam Bata Road, began in 1982 as the Escorts Heart Institute and Research Centre and joined Fortis Healthcare in 2005. It has a legacy of more than 40 years and is now a multispeciality hospital of about 210 beds with over 48 ICU beds, seven operating theatres and an advanced catheterisation laboratory. It was the first hospital in Faridabad to earn NABH accreditation, and later NABL accreditation.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers cardiology, cardiac surgery, neurosurgery, neurology, general surgery, orthopaedics, urology, critical care, pulmonology, ENT, nephrology, ophthalmology, plastic surgery, vascular surgery, paediatrics, general medicine, gastroenterology and obstetrics and gynaecology. Its cardiac services range from emergency and interventional cardiology, with rotational atherectomy, radial angioplasty, TAVI, ICD implants and leadless pacemakers, to open-heart surgery for bypass, valve, congenital and aortic conditions, and heart transplantation.\n##technology\nRecognitions include WSO Angels Diamond Status (2023) for stroke care, the Double Helical Award (2018) as the leading cardiac hospital in Haryana and a centre-of-excellence recognition in emergency medicine (2018). Centres of excellence include organ transplants and cardiac sciences.\n##international\nThe hospital serves patients from more than 50 countries through its international patient services programme. Faridabad is reached from Delhi by the Metro and highway.",
	'max-hospital':
		"##history\nMax Super Speciality Hospital, Gurugram, is located at B Block, Sushant Lok 1, near HUDA City Centre, in Sector 43. It is a compact superspeciality hospital of around 100 beds within the Max Healthcare network and has treated over half a million patients across 36 clinical specialities. It is accredited by NABH and NABL, has Green OT certification and has won awards including Best Multi-Speciality Hospital in Haryana (Double Helical Awards 2016) and Best Hospital for Patient Care in the North Region (Financial Express Healthcare Awards 2022).\n##specialities\nThe hospital provides medical and surgical oncology, cardiology, ENT, orthopaedics and joint replacement, nephrology, neurology and neurosurgery, urology and uro-oncology, minimal access and laparoscopic surgery, internal medicine, obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics, pulmonology, ophthalmology, dental care, infertility and IVF, emergency, aesthetic and reconstructive surgery and critical care. Notable doctors include Dr. S. K. S. Marya in orthopaedics and joint replacement, Dr. Arun Saroha in neurosciences and spine surgery and Dr. Amit Goel in urology and kidney transplant.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 12 adult ICU beds, PICU, NICU and cardiac care beds, endoscopy, radiology and pathology services, and recognition for advances in robotic surgery and transplant care.\n##international\nAs part of the Max network, the hospital cares for domestic and international patients. Its location beside HUDA City Centre Metro station makes it easy to reach from Delhi and Gurugram hotels.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-vaishali':
		"##history\nMax Super Speciality Hospital, Vaishali, in Ghaziabad is a premier multi-super speciality hospital of 387+ beds within the Max Healthcare network, on Ashok Marg near Vaishali Metro. It has won awards including Best Multi-Specialty Hospital in Delhi NCR (ET Now, 2019), Excellence in Patient Care (CIMS, 2018), Best Hospital in Quality Care (AHPI, 2017), Best Super Specialty Hospital in NCR (Times Health, 2016) and Best Hospital in North India (CNBC, 2015).\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers more than 37 clinical specialities, including oncology, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, orthopaedics, nephrology, kidney and liver transplant, gastroenterology, pulmonology, endocrinology, diabetes, urology and aesthetic and reconstructive surgery. Five institutes operate on its premises: the Max Institute of Cancer Care, Renal Sciences, Cardiac Sciences and Neurosciences, and the Max Trauma Centre.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 128 critical care beds, 16 high dependency beds and 14 high-end modular operation theatres, guided by more than 389 doctors and over 1,000 nursing and support staff. It is accredited by NABH and NABL.\n##international\nThe hospital offers dedicated international patient services including airport pickup and drop-off, interpreters, visa support, accommodation arrangements and an international patient lounge, and receives thousands of patients each year, particularly from Africa, SAARC, the GCC and CIS countries.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-noida':
		"##history\nMax Healthcare's hospital in Sector 128, Noida, was acquired by Max Healthcare in 2024 and was previously known as Jaypee Hospital. It spans more than 72,000 square metres, currently operates 500+ beds and plans to grow to 1,200 beds, and is one of the more advanced multispeciality hospitals in the Delhi-NCR region. It is easily reachable from Delhi, Noida and the Yamuna Expressway. Recognitions include India's Most Trusted Healthcare Award (2019) and the AHPI Digital/Smart Hospital Award (2023).\n##specialities\nThe hospital is known for cardiac sciences, oncology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, gastroenterology and renal care, and its multidisciplinary team covers cardiology, oncology, organ transplants, neurosciences, orthopaedics, respiratory and critical care, haematology, paediatrics and mother and child care. Max also operates a smaller multispeciality centre in Sector 19, Noida.\n##technology\nTechnology includes the da Vinci Xi robotic surgery system, the TrueBeam STx linear accelerator for precise cancer treatment, brachytherapy, 3.0 Tesla MRI, 128-slice CT and PET-CT with flow motion technology, plus a dual-head SPECT-CT. The hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL.\n##international\nThe hospital supports international patients with appointment planning, opinions and travel coordination.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-dwarka':
		"##history\nMax Super Speciality Hospital, Dwarka, is situated in South West Delhi on an 8.62-acre eco-friendly campus. It is one of the first five-star GRIHA-compliant green hospitals in Delhi NCR, combining sustainable design with a full range of tertiary services. It has more than 300 beds and is supported by 230+ doctors and over 650 trained staff.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers cardiac sciences, neurosciences, renal sciences, liver and gastrointestinal sciences, oncology, pulmonology, orthopaedics, bariatric and minimally invasive surgery, robotic surgery, ENT and cochlear implants, paediatrics, obstetrics and gynaecology, IVF, dermatology, psychiatry, endocrinology, diabetes management and emergency and trauma care.\n##technology\nIt has 120+ critical care beds, 10 high-end modular operation theatres, advanced endoscopy suites, a dedicated chemotherapy wing and more than 50 outpatient chambers, with over 20 emergency beds and a triage system. Technology includes the da Vinci surgical robot for oncology, urology, gynaecology and general surgery, a joint replacement system, a 3T MRI and a Philips Azurion cath lab for complex cardiac interventions, plus digital mammography. It is accredited by NABH.\n##international\nThe hospital has a dedicated international patient services team offering visa assistance, airport transfers, language interpreters, travel help and personalised care coordination. Dwarka is close to the airport and the Metro.",
	'max-super-speciality-hospital-shalimar-bagh':
		"##history\nMax Super Speciality Hospital, Shalimar Bagh, was established in 2011 and is a large multi-super speciality hospital in North West Delhi at FC-50, C and D Block. It is accredited by JCI and NABH and is part of the Max Healthcare network. Sources describe it as a 400-plus bed hospital.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers more than 37 clinical specialities, including cancer care, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, orthopaedics, nephrology and urology, and is known for treating complex conditions under one roof. Its centres bring together specialists in oncology, cardiac care, neurosciences, digestive and liver diseases, joint replacement and renal sciences.\n##technology\nAs a Max hospital, it offers modular operation theatres, critical care units, advanced imaging and laboratory services and 24/7 emergency care, supported by the group's clinical protocols and quality systems.\n##international\nMax Healthcare hospitals provide international patient services such as treatment planning, visa assistance, airport pickup, interpreters and accommodation support. Shalimar Bagh is in North West Delhi with Metro access.",
	'max-smart-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nMax Smart Super Speciality Hospital in Saket opened in 2013 as a unit of Gujarmal Modi Hospital and Research Center for Medical Sciences and shares a medical campus with Max Super Speciality Hospital, Saket, on Press Enclave Marg in the Saket Institutional Area. It is a 250-bed tertiary-care hospital with about 50 critical care beds.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers cardiac sciences, orthopaedics, urology, kidney transplant, neurology, neurosurgery, paediatrics, and obstetrics and gynaecology, and is a regional referral centre for complex operations such as neurovascular intervention, targeted cancer therapies, cardiac surgery, orthopaedic surgeries, and liver and kidney transplants.\n##technology\nThere are 12 high-end modular operating theatres, an emergency resuscitation and observation unit, a dedicated endoscopy unit and an advanced dialysis unit. Technology includes 3.0 Tesla MRI, 256-slice CT angio, cath labs with electrophysiology navigation, a flat panel C-arm detector, 4D echo, a digital orthopaedic suite, OCT, EEG, CRRT, DEXA and an intra-operative portable CT with navigation, plus the Mako robotic arm for joint replacement and the da Vinci Xi. It is NABH accredited.\n##international\nBeing on the same campus as Max Saket, the hospital benefits from the group's international patient services, which include treatment planning, visa assistance, airport pickup, interpreters and accommodation support.",
	'psri-hospital':
		"##history\nPushpawati Singhania Hospital & Research Institute (PSRI) was founded in 1996 by two AIIMS professors, Prof. B. N. Tandon and Prof. K. K. Malhotra, in Sheikh Sarai, South Delhi. It began with super-specialities in gastroenterology, GI surgery, nephrology and urology and has since grown into a comprehensive multispeciality hospital. It has been awarded as one of the best hospitals in Delhi NCR and is accredited by JCI and NABH, and its laboratories by NABL.\n##specialities\nPSRI offers cardiology and cardio-thoracic surgery, neurology and neurosurgery, gastroenterology and GI surgery, a liver transplant programme, orthopaedics and joint replacement, nephrology, urology and kidney transplant, pulmonology and sleep medicine, oncology and onco-surgery, internal medicine, gynaecology, ENT and general surgery. Its liver transplant team reports experience of more than 1,200 liver transplants, and its transplant programme covers liver, heart, kidney, bone marrow and corneal transplants. The hospital is particularly known for care of the liver, kidney, prostate, gall bladder, pancreas and gastrointestinal tract.\n##technology\nThe hospital offers 24/7 emergency services, a 24-hour pharmacy, ambulance service, blood bank, CT scan, radiology and X-ray, with a bed capacity that sources put at 200 to 250 or more.\n##international\nPSRI has an International Patient Centre with a team of dedicated international care experts who understand the needs of overseas patients and their families. It is on Press Enclave Marg in Sheikh Sarai, near Saket.",
	'venkateshwar-hospital':
		"##history\nVenkateshwar Hospital in Sector 18A, Dwarka, was established in 2016 and has become a leading healthcare provider in West Delhi. It is accredited by NABH and NABL and has received a range of awards, including Best Hospital in East Delhi (2018), Best for Patient Safety (2021), Best Multi-Specialty (2020), Best for Neurology (2017) and a Gold Award in the IGBC Green Healthcare category (2024).\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers services across 32 to 34 specialities, including cardiac sciences, oncology, neurology, orthopaedics, urology, transplants, gastroenterology and emergency medicine. Its centres of excellence are cardiac sciences, oncology and bone marrow transplant, renal sciences, neurosciences, and gastro sciences and liver transplant. It is one of India's leading urology centres offering robotic-assisted surgery.\n##technology\nThe hospital is equipped with the Hugo robotic-assisted surgery system, a 3 Tesla MRI, a 256-slice CT, PET-CT, mammography, interventional cath labs, gamma cameras, linear accelerators, DOTA scan and Fibroscan. It has more than 100 ICU beds and 10 modular operation theatres.\n##international\nThe hospital has a Department of International Service that supports international patients around the clock as a single point of contact, with assistance for visa, travel, accommodation, interpreter services and post-treatment continuity of care. It is about 12 km from the airport and opposite Dwarka Sector 12 Metro station.",
	'primus-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nPrimus Super Speciality Hospital, in the diplomatic enclave of Chanakyapuri, is a multispeciality hospital conceptualised around the latest global advances in medical technology, and is NABH and ISO certified. It carries several notable firsts: India's first binaural cochlear implant, and a global record for a partial hip replacement in a 107-year-old woman. Awards include Best Hospital for Neurology in Delhi (2021), Best Hospital for Oncology in Delhi (2020), Best Hospital for Cardiology in North India (2019) and Best Multi-Specialty Hospital in Delhi (2018).\n##specialities\nThe hospital provides care in orthopaedics, oncology, gastroenterology, ENT, haematology, physical medicine, cardiology, general surgery, nephrology, neurology, neurosurgery, transplant and urology. Specialised centres include the Primus Spine Centre and Orthopaedic Centre, the Minimal Access Surgery Centre, and the Neurology and Neurosurgery Centre. It performs more than 3,300 surgeries a year and treats over 45,000 outpatients.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 250 beds, 18 ICU beds and 6 high-dependency beds, seven modular operation theatres, a 15-bed dialysis unit and a flat-panel cath lab, with MRI, CT, blood bank, pharmacy and 24/7 emergency services.\n##international\nPrimus reports serving patients from more than 100 countries, and offers international patient facilities such as accommodation, flight booking, airport transfers and interpreters. Chanakyapuri is close to embassies and central Delhi hotels.",
	'ck-birla-hospital':
		"##history\nCK Birla Hospital in West Punjabi Bagh was founded in 2021 as the latest addition to the CKA Birla Group, which has served India's healthcare needs for more than 50 years. It describes itself as a modern, boutique multispeciality hospital in the heart of West Delhi, with 100+ well-appointed beds according to one source and more than 230 according to others, and a team of 60+ doctors. It reports having served more than 250,000 patients and performed over 10,000 surgeries, with a 95% patient satisfaction rate.\n##specialities\nThe hospital's services include mother and child care (obstetrics, gynaecology, neonatology and paediatrics, NICU, fetal medicine, fertility and IVF), advanced surgical sciences (minimally invasive surgery, gastrointestinal and bariatric surgery, vascular surgery, plastics and aesthetics, urology and gastroenterology), oncology (surgical and medical oncology, haematology, chemotherapy, genetic screening), orthopaedics (joint replacement, arthroscopy, trauma and sports injuries, spine, foot and ankle surgery) and family health services.\n##technology\nThe hospital has a Level III neonatal ICU, eight modular operating theatres, North India's first water-birthing facility and advanced robotic surgery, including a da Vinci surgical robot and an orthopaedic robot for knee replacement. It follows international protocols, including some adapted from the UK's NHS guidelines, and is accredited by NABH and NABL.\n##international\nThe hospital cares for both Indian and international patients. It is near Punjabi Bagh Metro station.",
	'narayana-hospital':
		"##history\nNarayana Superspeciality Hospital in Gurugram belongs to the Narayana Health group, founded by cardiac surgeon Dr. Devi Shetty, who has performed more than 15,000 heart operations and built one of India's largest hospital chains. The Gurugram hospital, at Plot 3201, Block V, DLF Phase III (Sector 24), is designed to meet national and international standards and is a top choice for patients from Africa, the Middle East, CIS and Southeast Asia seeking international-quality care at affordable cost.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is strong in cardiac sciences, with ECMO, heart transplant, robotic cardiac surgery, minimally invasive valve repair and replacement, TAVI, cardiac resynchronisation therapy and advanced coronary interventions such as angioplasty and stenting. Its team of cardiologists, interventional cardiologists and cardiac surgeons care for both adults and children. The wider group also runs centres of excellence in cancer care, neurosciences, orthopaedics, gastro sciences and renal sciences.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 215+ beds with advanced ICU and HDU facilities, more than 110 doctors across over 30 specialities, robotic surgery, precision oncology, a 3.0 Tesla MRI and an advanced cath lab. It is accredited by NABH.\n##international\nNarayana Gurugram supports international patients with affordable, protocol-driven care. Its location near Cyber City and the Golf Course Road corridor is convenient for Gurugram hotels.",
	'asian-institute-of-medical-sciences':
		"##history\nAsian Institute of Medical Sciences (Asian Hospital), Faridabad, was established in 2010 and is a 425-bed tertiary-care hospital accredited by NABH, NABL and AACI. It has been honoured as Delhi/NCR's leading private multi-speciality hospital for nine years in a row and rated among the top seven hospitals in Delhi NCR by The Week magazine over several years. It was the first hospital in Faridabad and Haryana to receive the YouTube Silver Play Button for more than 100,000 subscribers.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has 14 centres of excellence. The Asian Cancer Centre offers end-to-end services from prevention and early detection to treatment and palliative care, and was the first in North India to deploy Varian RapidArc on a Trilogy system, along with PET-CT, a dual-head gamma camera and HDR brachytherapy. The Asian Centre for Bone Marrow Transplant treats blood cancers and non-malignant conditions, and the hospital also runs renal transplant programmes. Other departments include cardiology and cardiac surgery, orthopaedics and spine, neurosciences, gastroenterology and hepatology, nephrology, urology, gynaecology, paediatrics and more.\n##technology\nThe hospital has advanced imaging, critical care and emergency and trauma services, and laboratory and rehabilitation support.\n##international\nAsian Hospital treats international patients, including a 15-year-old Iraqi girl with severe aplastic anaemia who received a matched unrelated German donor transplant, the first such case in Delhi NCR. Faridabad is reachable from Delhi by the Metro and highway.",
	'yatharth-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nYatharth Hospitals was established in 2008 by Dr. Ajay Kumar Tyagi and Dr. Kapil Kumar, with a 250-bed facility in Noida in 2013 and a third hospital in Noida Extension in 2019. The Noida Extension hospital is a 450-bed tertiary-care facility. It has received awards including Best Brand in Healthcare 2023 (ET Edge Best Brands Conclave), the National Healthcare Excellence Award and the Patient Safety Excellence Award.\n##specialities\nThe hospital specialises in cardiology, neurosciences, general surgery, nephrology, urology, paediatrics, gastroenterology, pulmonology, obstetrics and gynaecology, orthopaedics, spine, rheumatology, ENT, dermatology, ophthalmology, dentistry, psychiatry, anaesthesiology, physiotherapy, radiology, pathology and nutrition. Its centres of excellence cover cardiology, oncology, neurosciences, urology, nephrology, gastroenterology, general surgery, and spine and rheumatology.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 11 modular operation theatres and 125 critical care beds and offers the da Vinci X robotic system for minimally invasive surgery. It is the first and only hospital in Uttar Pradesh to earn JCI accreditation, and is also accredited by NABH.\n##international\nThe hospital offers airport pickups and local travel, medical visa support and lodging arrangements, dedicated medical coordinators, multilingual interpreters and customised dietary support. It is in Noida Extension (Greater Noida West).",
	'yashoda-super-speciality-hospitals':
		"##history\nYashoda Super Speciality Hospital in Kaushambi, Ghaziabad, established in 2006, is the flagship unit of the Yashoda Group of Hospitals in the NCR, serving East Delhi and western Uttar Pradesh. It started with 100 beds and is now a 300+ bed tertiary-care institution. It was the first hospital in Ghaziabad to receive NABH accreditation, alongside NABL accreditation for its laboratories.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers advanced care across more than 50 specialities, including neurosciences, cardiology and CTVS, joint replacement, paediatrics, nephrology and renal transplant, gastroenterology, general medicine, dentistry, orthopaedics, ophthalmology, pulmonology, oncology, obstetrics and gynaecology, urology, dermatology, endocrinology, physiotherapy, plastic surgery, psychiatry, rheumatology and audiology. Centres of excellence cover cardiology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, oncology and gastroenterology, and its cancer care programme adds palliative care, pain management, physiotherapy, nutrition counselling and psychological support. Its Cell and Gene Therapy Department focuses on advanced transfusion medicine and cellular therapies.\n##technology\nThe hospital has advanced modular operation theatres, a high-tech cath lab and dedicated ICUs, supported by 24/7 services.\n##international\nKaushambi is close to Kaushambi Metro station and Anand Vihar ISBT, making the hospital convenient to reach from central and East Delhi.",
	'saroj-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nSaroj Super Speciality Hospital in Sector 14, Rohini, has operated since 1997 and began as a Heart Institute, inaugurated in March 2001 by the then President of India, K. R. Narayanan. By 2015 it expanded its services and rebranded as Saroj Super Speciality Hospital. It is a 154+ bed multi-super speciality hospital in North West Delhi with a team of about 79 doctors across 16 specialities.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers super-speciality services in medicine, ENT, joint replacement, cardiac surgery, neurology, nephrology, minimal access surgery, neurosurgery, endocrinology, gastroenterology and cosmetic and reconstructive surgery. Other services include cancer care, oncology, chest surgery, ophthalmology, a centre for joint replacement and orthopaedics, laboratory services, child care, paediatric endocrinology, clinical psychology, and plastic, aesthetic and reconstructive surgery.\n##technology\nThe hospital has advanced cath lab units, operation theatres, an ultra-fast multi-slice CT scan, a non-invasive cardiac lab and technology for advanced laparoscopic surgery. It is accredited by NABH and NABL and ISO certified, and is on the panel of more than 100 organisations including insurance companies and TPAs. It is open 24/7.\n##international\nSaroj has a dedicated Center for International Patient Care that offers customised services and conveniences for patients from different countries. It is at Bhagwan Mahavir Marg near Madhuban Chowk.",
	'aakash-hospital':
		"##history\nAakash Hospital in Malviya Nagar, South Delhi, was founded in 2004 and has grown into a trusted local multi-speciality hospital. It is a NABH-accredited and ISO 9001:2000 certified hospital, functioning 24 hours a day, seven days a week. It is a compact 50-bed hospital with a small team of experienced doctors, including senior orthopaedic and obstetrics and gynaecology specialists with two to three decades of experience.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers internal medicine, general surgery, orthopaedics, obstetrics and gynaecology, ENT, paediatrics and neonatology, gastroenterology, pulmonology, dermatology, radiology and critical care. Round-the-clock services include ultrasound, laboratory tests, X-ray, ECG, Holter, Doppler, and TMT and echo. It also offers home healthcare and ambulance services, including ground and air ambulance.\n##technology\nThe hospital has modern diagnostic tools, advanced surgical units, round-the-clock emergency and pharmacy services. Patients can choose deluxe, air-conditioned or economy rooms, with an inbuilt pipeline providing oxygen and suction next to each bed.\n##international\nInternational patients have access to a range of exclusive services. Because of its size, Aakash Hospital is well suited to patients who need a defined procedure such as an orthopaedic, gynaecological or general surgical operation, or a supportive local base for follow-up. It is in Malviya Nagar, near Malviya Nagar Metro.\nPlease note that this is a different hospital from Aakash Healthcare Super Speciality Hospital in Dwarka.",
	'sci-international-hospital':
		"##history\nSCI International Hospital was established in 2014 in Greater Kailash Part 1, New Delhi, with the aim of developing a super-speciality surgical centre with the latest equipment and facilities. It is a 50-bed, NABH-accredited hospital and reports having treated more than 50,000 patients from six continents. It has delivered more than 2,500 babies from over 55 countries and is a trusted medical provider for embassies and international visitors.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is a centre of excellence for urology and andrology, IVF and fertility, gynaecology and obstetrics, advanced laparoscopic surgery, orthopaedics, joint replacement and sports injury, ENT and cochlear implants with speech therapy, neonatology, ophthalmology, and dentistry and orthodontics. Its urology and andrology team includes Dr. Gautam Banga, a reconstructive urologist, andrologist and penile implant surgeon with more than 20 years of specialised experience and over 3,000 complex urological surgeries.\n##technology\nThe hospital has four modular operating theatres and 15 critical care beds, with modern equipment and support services.\n##international\nSCI offers dedicated support for international and NRI patients, including treatment planning, consultation assistance and personalised care through the medical journey. Greater Kailash Part 1 is a well-served South Delhi neighbourhood with restaurants, hotels and Metro access.",
	'the-signature-advanced-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nThe Signature Advanced Super Speciality Hospital in Sector 37D, Gurugram, was established in 2019 under the Park Hospital network. Park Group was founded by Dr. Ajit Gupta, who started his professional journey in 1981 and opened the first hospital, Park Sunil Hospital in Malviya Nagar, in 1982. The group is now North India's second-largest hospital chain, with about 17 hospitals and roughly 4,300 beds across 15 cities. It was recently honoured at the Healthcare Pioneers of Delhi 2026 awards.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers cardiac sciences, orthopaedics and joint replacement, neurosciences, gastroenterology, renal sciences and kidney transplant, obstetrics and gynaecology, paediatrics, ENT, ophthalmology, dermatology, psychiatry, pathology, interventional radiology and physiotherapy.\n##technology\nWith about 150 beds, including critical care units, the hospital has MRI, CT, laboratories and a fully functional blood bank. It offers 24x7 emergency services, is NABH accredited and sits near the Dwarka Expressway, one of Gurugram's fast-developing healthcare corridors.\n##international\nThe Signature provides advanced multi-speciality and super-speciality care with modern technology and patient-focused infrastructure. Its location near the Dwarka Expressway makes it convenient for travellers arriving from the airport.",
	'sci-ivf-hospital':
		"##history\nSCI IVF Hospital is a fertility centre in Greater Kailash, Delhi, founded by Dr. Shivani Sachdev Gour and Dr. Vishal Dutt Gour as part of SCI Healthcare. Dr. Gour spent four years as a clinical research fellow in IVF at Hammersmith Hospital in London and worked as a gynaecologist and obstetrician at the Royal Infirmary of Edinburgh. In 2005 she became a member of the Royal College of Obstetricians and Gynaecologists (UK). The centre says it has helped patients from more than 55 countries reach parenthood.\n##specialities\nSCI IVF Hospital adheres to global clinical standards and offers IVF, ICSI, IUI, egg and embryo freezing, donor programmes and genetic testing under one roof, together with male and female infertility treatment. It reports success rates of 75 to 80 percent depending on patient age, medical condition and treatment type, and says rates can be higher for women younger than 35 using their own eggs. As with any clinic, success rates depend on the individual, so patients should ask for figures relevant to their own age and diagnosis.\n##technology\nThe centre has an embryology laboratory and offers personalised treatment plans, following the ethical standards set out by the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR) and the applicable Indian laws.\n##international\nInternational couples can plan consultations remotely and then travel for a defined treatment window. The centre is close to Greater Kailash and Kailash Colony hotels and Metro.",
	'nova-ivf-fertility':
		"##history\nNova IVF Fertility was established in 2011 and describes itself as India's first IVF chain to bring world-class standards of IVF treatment and embryology protocols to the country, in partnership with IVI of Spain. It now has around 70 centres across roughly 50 cities and more than 90 IVF specialists, and reports over 100,000 successful IVF pregnancies. It received the IVF/Fertility Champion of the Year award at the ETHealthworld National Fertility Awards 2025 and recognition from the Indian Society for Assisted Reproduction.\n##specialities\nNova offers IUI, IVF and ICSI, andrology, and advanced techniques such as vitrification of eggs and embryos, assisted hatching, blastocyst culture, embryoscope time-lapse imaging and ERA (endometrial receptivity array). It introduced Delhi's first IVF centre with an embryoscope. The group states an IVF/ICSI success rate of about 71 percent.\n##technology\nAll of its Delhi NCR clinics have advanced embryology laboratories, modern operating theatres and comfortable recovery areas following international protocols. The Delhi flagship is at B2/1A, Safdarjung Enclave, on Africa Avenue, and other clinics include Vasant Vihar and Rajouri Garden.\n##international\nNova IVF Fertility offers consultations for international couples. Its South Delhi locations are close to major hotels and the Metro.",
	'fortis-ridge-ivf-centre':
		"##history\nFortis Ridge IVF Centre has been part of Fortis Hospital, Shalimar Bagh, since 2010, on the first floor of A Block, Shaheed Udham Singh Marg. It brings together the Ridge IVF fertility team and the Fortis network, with a team of about 20 doctors, embryologists, andrologists, urologists, gynaecologists, surgeons and psychologists offering complete male and female infertility treatment. Its specialists include Dr. M. Gouri Devi, who has written several books on IVF, and Dr. Sonia Malik, who has more than 30 years of experience and has received the Dr. Kanak Goyal Award.\n##specialities\nThe centre offers a full spectrum of fertility treatments, from IVF, ICSI and IUI to fertility preservation programmes, egg and sperm donation, blastocyst transfer, preimplantation genetic testing and embryo freezing, which improve success rates and reduce risks. Fertility specialists, embryologists, nutritionists and wellness coaches work as one team so that the patient journey is medically sound and emotionally supported.\n##technology\nThe centre offers private consultation lounges and discreet scheduling, along with compassionate counselling and customised packages. Being inside a multi-super speciality hospital, it has access to Fortis Shalimar Bagh's obstetrics, neonatology, imaging and laboratory services.\n##international\nInternational patients can use the hospital's facilities for families, including accommodation for relatives and concierge services. Shalimar Bagh is in North West Delhi with Metro access.",
	'delhi-ivf-fertility-research-centre':
		"##history\nDelhi IVF & Fertility Research Centre is one of India's earliest and best-known IVF clinics and was founded by Dr. Anoop Kumar Gupta, who has treated infertility for decades. Dr. Gupta studied and trained abroad, including at the IVF Osaka Clinic in Japan, Liverpool Women's Hospital in the UK (ICSI training) and in Singapore (blastocyst culture). He is an active member of ESHRE, the American Society for Reproductive Medicine, FOGSI and the IMA, and has lectured and chaired sessions at international ART conferences representing India. The centre says he has treated patients from more than 55 nations.\n##specialities\nThe centre offers IVF-ET, IUI, ICSI, assisted hatching, blastocyst culture and egg and embryo donation. It reports helping over 11,000 to 21,000 couples in its history, depending on the source, and states that IVF success rates are typically 60 to 70 percent in women under 35 — a figure that will vary by individual. Its approach is described as slowing things down, understanding the couple's story and suggesting a plan that is medically sound and emotionally manageable.\n##technology\nThe clinic is equipped with one of the more advanced embryology laboratories in India. Its Mandi House clinic is in the Bengali Market and Tansen Marg area of central Delhi, near Mandi House Metro station.\n##international\nDelhi IVF offers programmes and coordinators for international patients, including assistance with visas, accommodation and translation.",
	'indira-ivf':
		"##history\nIndira IVF began as a two-room fertility clinic in Udaipur, Rajasthan, started by Dr. Ajay Murdia with just Rs 5,000, and named after his wife Indira. He opened one of India's first sperm banks in Udaipur and trained doctors from across the country. The Indira IVF group was founded in 2011, and his sons Dr. Kshitiz Murdia and Nitiz Murdia brought the services under the Indira IVF banner. It is now one of India's largest IVF chains, with more than 100 centres nationwide including Delhi and NCR, and reports helping over 200,000 couples.\n##specialities\nEach centre has its own embryology laboratory, dedicated specialists and the full range of fertility diagnostics and treatments, including IUI, IVF and ICSI. The group has more than 340 IVF doctors and states cumulative success rates across its network; individual outcomes depend on age, diagnosis and treatment type.\n##technology\nThe group's operating philosophy is built around awareness, accessibility and reliability, with a focus on reducing the stigma of infertility. Dr. Ajay Murdia has been recognised at the ETHealthworld National Fertility Awards.\n##international\nIndira IVF has centres in several parts of Delhi and NCR, so international patients can choose a clinic close to their hotel.",
	'cloudnine-ivf-centre-kailash-colony':
		"##history\nCloudnine Fertility in Kailash Colony, at A-18, Lala Lajpat Rai Road, is part of the Cloudnine Group of Hospitals, founded in 2007 by neonatologist Dr. R. Kishore Kumar. The group operates around 19 hospitals and clinics in cities including Bengaluru, Chennai, Pune, Gurugram, Mumbai and Chandigarh and has delivered more than 98,000 babies. It has received recognition such as the India Today Healthcare Excellence Awards (2018) and has been recognised for having advanced IVF and fertility centres.\n##specialities\nThe NABH-accredited centre provides IVF, ICSI, IVF with donor eggs, frozen embryo transfer, egg freezing (oocyte cryopreservation) and preimplantation genetic testing, with specialists who have more than 35 years of combined experience. Doctors include Dr. Ashima Gulia, a fertility specialist with over 17 years of experience in infertility and PCOS management and laparoscopic surgery, and Dr. Lavi Sindhu.\n##technology\nThe centre works alongside Cloudnine's maternity, gynaecology, paediatric and NICU services, and offers counselling to support emotional health during treatment. Emergency support and ambulance services are available around the clock.\n##international\nCloudnine offers international patient services including visa assistance, interpreters and travel coordination for fertility treatment. Kailash Colony is near Kailash Colony Metro station in South Delhi.",
	'international-fertility-centre':
		"##history\nInternational Fertility Centre (IFC), headquartered in New Delhi, is one of India's oldest fertility clinics and a network of more than 10 IVF clinics in India and Nepal. It was founded by Dr. Rita Bakshi, the chairperson, who has more than 37 years of experience as an infertility specialist and has helped families conceive thousands of IVF babies. The Green Park centre is at H-6, First Floor, near the Main Market in Green Park.\n##specialities\nThe centre offers advanced IVF, ICSI, IUI, egg and sperm donation and PGD/PGS, as well as expertise in recurrent miscarriage, endometriosis and ovulatory disorders, and endoscopy for women's health. Dr. Bakshi performs more than 1,000 IVF and ICSI cycles a year at the head office, and the centre reports success rates above 50 percent, a figure that depends on each patient's age and diagnosis.\n##technology\nIFC is described as a super-specialised centre with a state-of-the-art IVF laboratory, operating theatre and equipment, providing treatment for women's health, especially infertility and endoscopy, at affordable prices.\n##international\nAs an established chain with an international network, IFC regularly treats overseas couples. Green Park has hotels, restaurants and Metro access.",
	'laimaa-fertility-ivf-surrogacy-clinic':
		"##history\nLaimaa Fertility was established in 2022 by a team of experienced embryologists and doctors and is located at E-580, Greater Kailash Part II, New Delhi. It emerged under the leadership of embryologist Pooja Agarwal, Dr. Akanksha Chauhan and Dr. Mamta Chahar, with Dr. Vineet Malhotra also on the team, combining medical and laboratory expertise. Emb. Pooja Agarwal began her career at Fortis Ridge IVF Centre and went on to lead IVF laboratories at several institutions, including in Gurugram and Noida, and is a certified embryologist for embryo biopsy.\n##specialities\nThe clinic offers IVF, ICSI, IUI, egg and embryo freezing, egg donation, tailored medication plans, minimally invasive surgical procedures for infertility and hormone therapy. It is known for its work with challenging cases such as low AMH and severe male-factor infertility, and its embryology team performs TESA-ICSI, PICSI, blastocyst transfer and egg and embryo freezing. Patients frequently praise Dr. Akanksha Chauhan for her kindness, knowledge and availability.\n##technology\nThe clinic uses advanced reproductive techniques and emphasises personalised care and ethical practice. As a newer clinic, it operates as a focused fertility centre with an in-house embryology lab.\n##international\nThe clinic offers consultations in English and Hindi. Greater Kailash Part II is a well-served South Delhi neighbourhood with hotels and Metro access.",
	'gaudium-ivf':
		"##history\nGaudium IVF and Women Health was founded in 2009 by Dr. Manika Khanna, a globally recognised infertility specialist and laparoscopic surgeon with more than 20 years of experience in fertility treatment. She received the Delhi Ratan Award in 2008 from the then President of India, and has been honoured with awards including the Rajiv Gandhi Excellence Award and Women Achievers' Award. Gaudium now has around 36 centres across six Indian states and centres in other countries, and reports healthy Gaudium babies in over 30 countries.\n##specialities\nThe centre provides IVF, egg freezing and embryo freezing, and is known for treating recurrent IVF failure, male-factor infertility, endometriosis and high-risk pregnancies. Dr. Khanna reports more than 10,000 IVF treatments to her credit, and the group's clinics are described as super-speciality clinics with multidisciplinary care and experienced embryologists.\n##technology\nGaudium's embryology ecosystem uses AI-powered tools, including SiD for sperm assessment and ERICA for embryo evaluation, at the heart of its Signature Lab framework that combines advanced embryology with internationally benchmarked quality standards. The Delhi clinic is at M-1, First Floor, South Extension Part 2.\n##international\nGaudium has treated couples from over 30 countries. South Extension is a busy South Delhi market district with good Metro connectivity.",
	'pristyn-care-ferticity-super-speciality-ivf-hospital':
		"##history\nPristyn Care Ferticity Super Speciality & IVF Hospital is located at 12, Navjeevan Vihar, Geetanjali Enclave, Malviya Nagar, New Delhi, and reports having helped more than 40,000 families worldwide. Its co-founder and director, Dr. Ila Gupta, has more than 29 years of experience in infertility treatment and assisted reproductive technologies, has handled more than 5,500 complex cases, and received the Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Health Award in 2023. The clinic is listed in the ICMR ART Clinics Registry.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is designed for couples seeking IVF, IUI, ICSI, egg freezing, embryo freezing and donor-based treatments. It manages PCOS, tubal block, low ovarian reserve, male-factor infertility, endometriosis and recurrent pregnancy loss, and offers ovulation induction and detailed hormonal and reproductive health assessments. Dr. Gupta reports success rates of up to 78 percent using techniques such as platelet-rich plasma therapy and genetic screening, though results vary from patient to patient.\n##technology\nAll fertility specialists are registered with the medical council, and the clinic runs as a super-speciality and IVF hospital with operating facilities, embryology laboratory and counselling support. It is open Monday to Saturday.\n##international\nThe clinic has treated international couples, including patients who travelled from the United States for IVF with Dr. Gupta. Malviya Nagar is near Malviya Nagar Metro station in South Delhi.",
	'nova-ivf-fertility-centre-rajouri-garden':
		"##history\nNova IVF Fertility's Rajouri Garden centre is one of the group's Delhi clinics, at GN-14, Shivaji Enclave, Sector G, Mehta Chowk, near Rajouri Garden Metro. Nova IVF Fertility was established in 2011, and the group received the Best IVF Chain in India award at the ET Healthworld National Fertility Awards in 2021 and the IVF/Fertility Champion of the Year award in 2025. The group reports more than 85,000 to 100,000 IVF live births across its network.\n##specialities\nThe clinic offers IUI, IVF, ICSI and MACS sperm selection, egg freezing, donor programmes and advanced diagnostics, and treats male infertility, unexplained infertility, low ovarian reserve, PCOS, endometriosis and tubal-factor infertility. Dr. Aswati Nair is an IVF specialist who completed her MBBS in Mumbai and MD in obstetrics and gynaecology, followed by an FNB in reproductive medicine, with more than 17 years of experience. She won the best paper award at the ISAR Kerala chapter for research on embryo glue in recurrent implantation failure. Dr. Meenakshi Banerjee, a gynaecologist with over 20 years of experience, also practises here.\n##technology\nLike other Nova IVF clinics in Delhi NCR, it has an advanced embryology laboratory, modern operating theatre and comfortable recovery area, following international protocols. The clinic is open from Monday to Saturday.\n##international\nRajouri Garden is well connected by Metro to central Delhi and the airport line.",
	'elixir-fertility-centre':
		"##history\nElixir Fertility Centre was established in 2014 and is an IVF and fertility clinic in North Delhi at Vardhman Royal Plaza, Plot 5, LSC Gujranwala Town-1. It aims to combine experienced infertility experts with advanced technology to improve success rates, and its IVF specialists and embryologists have trained at leading centres in the UK, Germany, Singapore and India.\n##specialities\nThe centre offers IVF, ICSI, IUI, semen analysis and genetic screening. Its team includes Dr. Puneet Kochhar, an IVF specialist who previously worked at Bourn Hall Clinic in Cambridge, UK, and taught at Lady Hardinge Medical College in Delhi; Dr. Pranay Ghosh, director and fertility consultant, who trained at centres including NURTURE in Nottingham, NUH CREST in Singapore and the Centre of Reproductive Medicine in Kiel, and completed a master's in the UK with distinction; Dr. Rajiv Singla, a reproductive endocrinologist; and Dr. Teita Ghosh, a clinical geneticist and reproductive immunologist.\n##technology\nThe clinic has a diagnostic laboratory, ultrasound, emergency service and parking, and works Monday to Saturday between about 9 am and 6 pm. It reports IVF success rates in the range of 65 to 75 percent, which will vary by individual circumstances.\n##international\nGujranwala Town in North Delhi is near Model Town and Kamla Nagar and is reached by Metro from central Delhi.",
	'femmenest-fertility-ivf-centre':
		"##history\nFemmenest is a premium women's healthcare centre in East Delhi providing IVF, infertility and gynaecology services, at C-52 UGF, Anand Vihar, opposite Pushpanjali Medical Centre. The centre is headed by Dr. Sowjanya Aggarwal, an IVF specialist and gynaecological laparoscopic and robotic surgeon with more than 20 years of clinical experience. She completed her MS in obstetrics and gynaecology at Sri Ramachandra University, Chennai, followed by a fellowship in minimal access gynaecological surgery and reproductive medicine in Kochi, and received the Dr. Jagdishwari Mishra Oration Award in 2012.\n##specialities\nThe centre provides IVF, IUI and ICSI, personalised support for couples, complete infertility care from diagnosis to hormonal therapies, and advanced gynaecology care for PCOS, hormonal imbalances, fertility concerns and routine women's health check-ups, along with fetal medicine. It has a team of senior doctors, clinical embryologists, support staff and dedicated nurses.\n##technology\nThe centre is equipped with state-of-the-art facilities for complete women's care. It is usually open Monday to Saturday from 9 am to 8 pm and on Sunday mornings, and has been rated highly by patients.\n##international\nAnand Vihar is well connected by Metro and by the Anand Vihar railway terminus and bus terminal, which is convenient for travellers arriving from other cities.",
	'india-ivf-clinic':
		"##history\nIndia IVF Clinic, in Vasant Vihar, is a fertility clinic in the Fortis network. It practises with a consulting presence at Fortis Flt. Lt. Rajan Dhall Hospital in Vasant Kunj, and is listed with an address at 35, Second Floor, Community Centre, Basant Lok, Vasant Vihar. It has been in healthcare for around 12 years and is rated highly by patients.\n##specialities\nDr. Richika Sahay leads the fertility team. She has more than 20 years of experience as a fertility specialist and gynaecological laparoscopic surgeon, is a certified reproductive endocrinologist and infertility (IVF-ICSI) sub-specialist, graduated from medical school with a gold medal and received the Best Young IVF Specialist award in 2018. Her areas of expertise include IVF and ICSI, egg and embryo freezing, ovulation induction, IUI, preimplantation genetic testing and screening, and conception and miscarriage management. She takes a holistic approach, with attention to nutrition, lifestyle and environment.\n##technology\nThe clinic is wheelchair accessible with parking. Patients describe the staff as friendly, caring and supportive, and mention successful pregnancies and births.\n##international\nBecause the team also works from Fortis Vasant Kunj, close to the international airport, international couples can combine fertility consultations with a well-equipped multispeciality hospital.",
	'spruce-dental':
		"##history\nSpruce Dental in Jasola Vihar, South Delhi, is part of the Spruce Dental group of clinics, led by implantologist and orthodontist Dr. Javed Rizwan, and is an ISO 9001:2015 certified clinic. It is at 122, Pocket 2, Jasola, near the DAV School, and is rated well by patients. Dr. Rizwan holds a BDS and MDS and pursued a master's in strategic implantology under a pioneer of corticobasal implantology in Munich, Germany. He has more than 15,000 implants to his credit and more than 500 full-mouth immediate implant cases.\n##specialities\nThe clinic provides pain-free root canal therapy to save damaged teeth, full-mouth dental implants for missing teeth, single-tooth implants, professional teeth whitening, advanced orthodontic options and smile makeovers with cosmetic dentistry. The group runs clinical residency programmes in general dentistry and implantology.\n##technology\nDigital imaging gives clear views of teeth and gums for better treatment planning, and the clinic aims to deliver ethical, patient-first dental care in a comfortable environment.\n##international\nJasola Vihar is close to Indraprastha Apollo Hospital and Jasola Metro stations in South Delhi. Dental implant and smile-design work is often planned in a small number of visits.",
	'zemya-ivf-fertility-clinics':
		"##history\nZemya IVF & Fertility Clinics is a fertility centre at C-10, Green Park Extension, New Delhi, described as one of the leading IVF centres in Delhi NCR. It offers empathic, patient-centred care and reports having helped more than 50,000 couples. Its team includes globally trained IVF experts and ESHRE-certified embryologists, including a senior embryologist and IVF lab manager with over 15 years of experience in clinical embryology and assisted reproductive technologies.\n##specialities\nZemya provides IVF, ICSI and IUI, male infertility care, egg freezing and fertility preservation under one roof, with personalised treatment plans. Its treatment pages cover IVF, ICSI and male infertility in detail.\n##technology\nFacilities include large waiting rooms, private and luxury recovery rooms, modular operating theatres, a modern IVF laboratory, an advanced andrology laboratory for male fertility tests, an own pharmacy, a pathology laboratory, an international patients' lounge, a counselling room, a conference room and video consultation services.\n##international\nGreen Park is a well-connected South Delhi neighbourhood with Metro access, hotels and restaurants, and the clinic has a lounge for international patients.",
	'kokilaben-dhirubhai-ambani-hospital':
		"##history\nKokilaben Dhirubhai Ambani Hospital, at Rao Saheb Achutrao Patwardhan Marg in Andheri West, Mumbai, became operational in early 2009 as a 750-bed multi-specialty hospital. It serves Mumbai, neighbouring regions and international patients and is accredited by JCI, NABH and CAP. In 2025 it was named Best Hospital – National in six categories (multispecialty, oncology, robotics, neurology, orthopaedics and rehabilitation) at the Financial Express Healthcare Summit and Awards, and received the NABH Digital Health Excellence Award.\n##specialities\nThe hospital reports more than 21,000 complex cancer surgeries, over 280 liver transplants and more than 3,600 robotic surgeries, performed by a team of over 400 doctors across departments. Its Centre for Robotic Surgery, set up in 2012, is described as the fastest to reach 1,000 robotic surgeries within 48 months of launch. Oncology, neurosciences, orthopaedics, cardiac sciences, transplants and rehabilitation are among its main strengths.\n##technology\nThe hospital has around 180 ICU beds and was the site of several firsts, including Asia's first three-room intra-operative MRI suite (IMRIS), Asia's first EDGE radiosurgery system from Varian and India's first spine surgery suite with an O-arm. It uses the da Vinci Xi and India's first Toumai robotic surgery system, which offers 3D HD visualisation and telesurgery capability.\n##international\nKokilaben is known for its international patient care, with concierge services and assistance for all medical travel needs. Andheri West is close to the Metro and to Mumbai's international airport.",
	'p-d-hinduja-hospital':
		"##history\nP. D. Hinduja Hospital was founded in 1951 by Parmanand Deepchand Hinduja in collaboration with the Massachusetts General Hospital, the main teaching hospital of Harvard Medical School, and moved into its East Wing building at the Mahim site in 1963, transforming it from a modest outpatient facility into a full-fledged hospital. It is on Veer Savarkar Marg, near Shivaji Park. It became the first hospital in India to receive the Green and Clean Hospital Platinum Certificate from Bureau Veritas, and has won awards including the IMC Ramkrishna Bajaj National Award for healthcare quality.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers services in more than 45 specialities except obstetrics, with 53 critical care beds, 19 day-care units, 170 consultants and more than 800 nurses and other staff, together with a health screening centre. It was the first private hospital in Mumbai to perform a cadaver kidney transplant and a peripheral blood stem cell transplant, and the first in India to perform an awake craniotomy for epilepsy surgery. Cardiology, oncology, neurology and orthopaedics are among its main strengths.\n##technology\nThe hospital runs DNB courses in 26 specialities, MSc and PhD programmes, a nursing college and allied health courses, and collaborates with institutions such as Hôpitaux Universitaires de Genève, Stanford University and Henry Ford Health. It is accredited by NABH.\n##international\nThe hospital has a dedicated international patient services department to help plan and coordinate treatment. Mahim is well connected by rail and road to central Mumbai and the airport.",
	'fortis-hospital-mulund':
		"##history\nFortis Hospital, Mulund, opened in 2002 and is a 400-bed multi-specialty quaternary-care hospital on the Mulund–Goregaon Link Road. It is described as the first hospital in India and South Asia to receive JCI accreditation and the only hospital in Western India with seven consecutive JCI accreditations. It was the first in the country to receive NABH accreditation for its emergency services and the first in India to launch an electronic ICU. The hospital has earned more than 250 awards for healthcare excellence.\n##specialities\nFortis Mulund houses Maharashtra's largest transplant centre for multi-organ transplants, covering kidney, liver, heart and bone marrow. It was the first in Western India to complete more than 100 heart transplants in just four years and completed its 100th bone marrow transplant in 2024. Its neurosciences programme, with advanced neuro-imaging and neuro-critical care units, is regarded as one of the best in India, and it also offers cardiac sciences, oncology, nephrology, urology, orthopaedics, gastroenterology, emergency and critical care and maternity care.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 108 ICU beds, six dedicated bone marrow transplant units and a Level 1 trauma centre. Oncology uses the Versa HD linear accelerator, and the hospital is among a few in the country with this radiation platform.\n##international\nFortis Mulund runs a 24/7 International Patient Unit that supports patients and families throughout the medical journey. It is in Mumbai's eastern suburbs, close to Mulund railway station.",
	'jaslok-hospital':
		"##history\nJaslok Hospital & Research Centre, at Dr. G. Deshmukh Marg on Peddar Road, was founded by philanthropist Seth Lokoomal Chanrai and surgeon Shantilal Jamnadas Mehta and was inaugurated on 6 July 1973 by Prime Minister Indira Gandhi. It is one of the oldest tertiary-care multi-specialty trust hospitals in India, and celebrated 50 years of service with the Navbharat Healthcare Award in 2022.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has about 50 specialities and nearly 20 specialty clinics, with more than 350 beds including 75+ ICU beds. It performed the first renal transplant in a private hospital in India in 1974, launched India's first private urology department, and achieved Mumbai's first private liver transplant in 1998 and Western India's first paediatric liver transplant. It introduced India's first triple-head gamma camera and solid-state cardiac camera, and was first in Mumbai with 2D echocardiography, electrophysiology and drug-eluting stents. In reproductive medicine it reports the world's first Cumulus Aided Transfer in IVF, and it won the Best IVF Clinic award at the ET Healthcare Fertility Awards in 2019.\n##technology\nThe hospital is accredited by NABH (5th edition), NABL and holds ISO 9001, 14001 and 45001 certifications, along with NABH nursing excellence and ethics committee accreditation.\n##international\nJaslok provides support for international patients including pre-arrival consultation and cost planning with teleconsultations and detailed treatment plans, and visa and travel assistance. It is in south Mumbai near Mahalaxmi.",
	'nanavati-max-super-speciality-hospital':
		"##history\nNanavati Max Super Speciality Hospital in Vile Parle was inaugurated in November 1950 by India's first Prime Minister, Jawaharlal Nehru, blessed by Mahatma Gandhi, and opened to patients in 1951. It has been a pillar of Mumbai's healthcare for more than 70 years and is now part of Max Healthcare. It has 350 beds, more than 350 consultants, over 100 resident doctors, around 475 nursing staff and about 1,500 employees.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has 55 speciality departments and centres of excellence in cardiology, oncology, nephrology, orthopaedics, spine surgery, neurology, bariatrics and surgical gastroenterology. It also offers physiotherapy, dermatology, plastic surgery, paediatric neurology, pulmonology, minimally invasive spine surgery, bone marrow transplant, obstetrics and gynaecology, digestive and liver care, general and laparoscopic surgery, joint replacement and neurosciences. It launched its Centre for Robotic Surgery in 2019 and introduced apomorphine pen and pump therapy for Parkinson's disease in collaboration with King's College London in 2018.\n##technology\nThe imaging centre spans more than 10,000 square feet with a 3 Tesla wide-bore MRI and a 64-slice PET-CT scanner with cardiac capability. The hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL, and has won awards including Best Hospital for Patient Safety (2021) and Hospital of the Year in Organ Transplant (2024).\n##international\nThe hospital has a dedicated International Patient Desk offering complimentary airport pickup and drop-off, visa assistance, medical travel insurance coordination, interpreters and translation, foreign currency exchange and customised meals. It is in Vile Parle West near Mumbai's domestic and international airports.",
	'apollo-hospitals-greams-road':
		"##history\nApollo Hospitals, Greams Road, was started in 1983 by Dr. Prathap C. Reddy as the first professionally run 150-bed private hospital in India, and as the country's first corporate hospital it played an important role in transforming private healthcare. Dr. Reddy was conferred the Padma Vibhushan and received lifetime achievement awards from three media houses. Today the hospital has 550 beds, is accredited by JCI and NABH and is widely considered one of the best hospitals in India for international patients.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has more than 12 centres of excellence, including the Apollo Heart Institute, the Institute of Liver Sciences, the Institute of Neurosciences, the Institute of Colorectal Surgery and the Institute of Robotic Surgery. Its transplant programme covers liver, kidney, heart and lung, with milestones such as the first successful pancreas transplant in India and Asia's first en-bloc combined heart and liver transplant. It was the first in India to introduce coronary angioplasty, stereotactic radiotherapy and radiosurgery for brain tumours.\n##technology\nTechnology includes the da Vinci robotic surgical system, ExcelsiusGPS for spine surgery, TrueBeam STx for radiation therapy, the first CyberKnife in India and the use of 64-slice PET-CT in Southeast Asia. The proton therapy centre is described as India's first and South Asia's most advanced.\n##international\nApollo Chennai has been recognised as Most Promising Company for International Medical Services (MT India Healthcare Awards, 2023). It is on Greams Lane off Greams Road in central Chennai, close to hotels.",
	'miot-international':
		"##history\nMIOT International, the Madras Institute of Orthopaedics and Traumatology, was started by Padmashri Prof. Dr. P. V. A. Mohandas on 12 February 1999 as a 70-bed hospital focused on orthopaedics and trauma care. Dr. Mohandas performed the first hip replacement surgery in India and received the Padmashri in 1992 for pioneering joint replacement. The hospital has since grown into a 1,000-bed quaternary-care hospital in Manapakkam with 63 specialities and 21 operation theatres, welcoming patients from more than 130 countries.\n##specialities\nMIOT's orthopaedics and joint replacement department has been ranked first in India by Outlook Health, with more than 40,000 joint replacements of the hip, knee and upper limbs. Milestones include the first keyhole surgery, India's first kidney transplant across blood groups, India's first haploidentical bone marrow transplant and the first TrueBeam STx radiotherapy installation in Asia Pacific. Since 2012 the MIOT International Centre has housed oncology, radiation oncology, a liver transplant centre and a bone marrow transplant centre, alongside cardiology, nephrology, neurosurgery, plastic surgery, paediatrics and obstetrics.\n##technology\nThe hospital is accredited by NABH and NABL and has won awards including Times Healthcare Legends in Orthopaedics and Best Multi-Speciality Hospital in Chennai (2018), the Radio City ICON Award (2019) and Times Healthcare Achievers Awards (2020).\n##international\nMIOT provides visa invitation letters, complimentary airport transportation and multilingual interpreter support. It is on Mount Poonamallee Road, not far from Chennai's airport.",
	'gleneagles-global-health-city':
		"##history\nGleneagles Global Health City in Perumbakkam, Chennai, is part of IHH Healthcare and one of India's largest multi-organ transplant and quaternary-care hospitals, on a 21-acre campus. Its Institute of Liver Disease and Transplantation, started in 2009 by Prof. Mohamed Rela, has performed more than 1,500 liver transplants and is regarded as one of the largest liver transplant programmes in India. Prof. Rela has performed more than 4,000 liver transplants and is listed in the Guinness Book of Records for a liver transplant on a five-day-old baby.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has 40+ specialities and is internationally recognised for organ transplantation, oncology, hepatology, neurosciences and trauma care. It performs liver, kidney, heart, lung and bone marrow transplants, and says it was the first in South India to perform five organ transplants in a single day, the first in India to conduct an adult swap liver transplant and a split-liver transplant, and the first in India to implant an artificial lung and perform a uterine transplant. Its lung transplant programme is considered among the best in India, and it performs liver transplants in collaboration with King's College Hospital, London.\n##technology\nThe hospital reports capacity of around 1,000 beds and is accredited by NABH and NABL, with halal certification for food.\n##international\nThe hospital aims to offer facilities that meet international standards at cost-effective prices, particularly for multi-organ transplantation. Perumbakkam is in South Chennai near the IT corridor.",
	'fortis-malar-hospital':
		"##history\nFortis Malar Hospital in Adyar, Chennai, was established in 1992 as Malar Hospital and became part of Fortis Healthcare in 2007. It is a 180-bed multi-specialty tertiary-care hospital offering care in over 40 specialities. It is known for its Fortis Centre for Heart Failure and Transplant, described as India's first comprehensive centre for heart failure management.\n##specialities\nThe hospital's cardiac programme spans interventional, invasive, non-invasive and paediatric cardiology, cardiovascular surgery and heart transplantation. The centre has completed more than 50 heart transplants, long-term LVAD implants and veno-arterial ECMO support for critical heart failure, and is credited with India's first successful Heartmate II LVAD and HVAD implants. Dr. K. R. Balakrishnan, director of cardiac sciences, has more than 30 years of experience, has performed more than 16,000 heart operations, and received the FICCI Special Jury Award. The hospital also offers neurology, neurosurgery, orthopaedics, nephrology, gynaecology, gastroenterology, urology, paediatrics and diabetes care.\n##technology\nThe hospital is accredited by NABH. Bed capacity figures vary between sources, so patients should confirm current capacity when planning.\n##international\nThe hospital treats patients from abroad; a recent case involved a successful heart transplant for a 40-year-old Pakistani national. Adyar is a quiet residential area of south Chennai.",
	'kauvery-hospital':
		"##history\nKauvery Hospital in Alwarpet, at 81, TTK Road, is a multispeciality hospital in central Chennai, part of the Kauvery group, which has more than 2,000 beds across 10 locations in Tamil Nadu and Karnataka. The hospital is described as being among the top 20 hospitals in India by Newsweek and has spent 25 years building a network with internationally trained surgeons. Its Alwarpet and Vadapalani hospitals hold JCI accreditation, described as India's only dual 8th-edition JCI network.\n##specialities\nKauvery has centres of excellence in cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, organ transplantation, orthopaedics and women's health. The Kauvery Heart Institute in Alwarpet focuses on complex angioplasty, Impella, hybrid bypass surgery and heart transplants. Its heart and lung transplant team, made up of transplant surgeons, heart-failure cardiologists, transplant pulmonologists, thoracic anaesthetists, intensivists, perfusionists and coordinators, was honoured by the Tamil Nadu State Transplant Authority (TRANSTAN) in 2023.\n##technology\nThe Kauvery Institute of Robotic Surgery offers da Vinci robotic surgery across oncology, urology, gastrointestinal, colorectal and cardiac surgery, liver surgery and kidney transplantation. The hospital has about 300 beds in a seven-floor building near the Alwarpet flyover and is accredited by NABH.\n##international\nWhat brings many international patients to Kauvery is its highly specialised medical team. Alwarpet is well placed in central Chennai near hotels and restaurants.",
	'manipal-hospital-old-airport-road':
		"##history\nManipal Hospital, Old Airport Road, was launched in Bengaluru in 1991 as the first corporate hospital in the city and has become the flagship of the Manipal Hospitals network and the cornerstone of the Manipal Education and Medical Group. It has been named Best Multispeciality Hospital (Private) at The Week Health Summit 2025 and Best Multi-Speciality Hospital in Bengaluru at The Week Best Hospitals Awards 2024, and won the Golden Peacock National Quality Award in 2005. It is accredited by NABH and JCI.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers more than 60 super-specialities with centres of excellence in oncology, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, orthopaedics and organ transplants. It is an established centre for multi-organ transplants, with comprehensive programmes for kidney, liver, pancreas, heart, lung and bone marrow, and is known for early adoption of robotic-assisted kidney transplantation in India. The wider network's transplant programme is among the largest in the country.\n##technology\nThe hospital has around 600 or more beds, including 144 intensive care beds, and 20 modular operation theatres, along with advanced cancer care and organ transplant units.\n##international\nThe hospital serves patients from more than 80 countries and provides end-to-end support including pre-arrival consultation and treatment planning with teleconsultations, visa and travel assistance with medical visa invitation letters, airport pickup and drop-off, accommodation, translation and multilingual interpreters. It is on HAL Old Airport Road.",
	'sakra-world-hospital':
		"##history\nSakra World Hospital in Bengaluru was launched in February 2014 and is described as India's first Japanese multispeciality hospital and India's first 100 percent foreign-direct-investment hospital, owned and managed by a joint venture between Toyota Tsusho and Secom Hospitals of Japan, with Kirloskar involved at launch. It combines the strengths of India and Japan, and its nursing protocols blend Indian and Japanese practice. It has received the Award for Excellence in Healthcare from the Indian Business Awards, national recognition from the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, and the first National Award for Laboratory Excellence from QCI. It has also achieved AACI accreditation, with a second 500-bed hospital announced.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers neurology, cardiology, orthopaedics, obstetrics and gynaecology, renal sciences, rehabilitation sciences, paediatrics, spine surgery, radiology, clinical psychology, internal medicine, ENT, head and neck surgery, cancer, blood disorders, plastic surgery, respiratory medicine, rheumatology, endocrinology, dentistry, dermatology, psychiatry, ophthalmology, critical care, pain medicine and more. It is renowned for cardiology, orthopaedics, neurology and organ transplants. The Sakra Institute of Rehabilitation Sciences is said to be the largest rehabilitation centre in Asia and the first with a global quality accreditation.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 350 inpatient beds, with imaging that includes MRI, multidetector CT, 3D and 4D ultrasound, digital X-ray, OPG and bone mineral densitometry.\n##international\nA dedicated International Patient Services department looks after patients and companions coming from overseas, with visa arrangements, airport transfers, accommodation, language interpretation and personalised care management. The hospital is on the Outer Ring Road near Marathahalli and Bellandur.",
	'narayana-institute-of-cardiac-sciences':
		"##history\nNarayana Institute of Cardiac Sciences was commissioned in 2000 as part of NH Health City in Bommasandra, Bengaluru, by cardiac surgeon Dr. Devi Shetty, the founder of Narayana Health. It is the flagship cardiac centre of Narayana Health and one of the largest cardiac hospitals in the world, part of a campus described as one of the world's largest cardiac care sites. The institute has performed more than 100,000 cardiac procedures and has a team of more than 250 cardiologists and cardiac specialists. It is accredited by JCI and NABH.\n##specialities\nThe institute specialises in cardiac surgery and heart transplantation and also provides electrophysiology services, left ventricular assist device (LVAD) implantation, transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) and a programme for structural heart conditions. It performs more than 40 cardiac surgeries per day, including around 16 paediatric heart surgeries.\n##technology\nThe facility has around 20 cardiac operating theatres, including two advanced robotic theatres, and several digital catheterisation laboratories, including a hybrid lab for interventional procedures and complex heart surgeries. It has about 200 critical care beds for post-operative care.\n##international\nThe institute is about 50 km from Kempegowda International Airport, and is convenient for patients travelling from other parts of India and abroad. It sits on Hosur Road near Electronic City.",
	'fortis-hospital-bannerghatta-road':
		"##history\nFortis Hospital, Bannerghatta Road, opened in 2006 and is Fortis Healthcare's flagship multi-specialty hospital in South India, opposite IIM Bangalore. It is accredited by NABH (four times) and JCI (five times) and is reported to be the first hospital in Karnataka to earn JCI accreditation. It has won awards including AHPI awards, the National Energy Conservation Award (2014), the Asian Patient Safety Award and international medical tourism accreditation for excellence in care, and has been ranked among the best multi-specialty hospitals in Bengaluru by The Week.\n##specialities\nThe hospital provides super-specialty tertiary care across about 40 medical fields, with centres of excellence in cardiology and cardiac surgery, neurology and neurosurgery, oncology, orthopaedics, organ transplant, gastroenterology, paediatrics and critical care. Its oncology department offers advanced radiotherapy, chemotherapy, tumour boards and bone marrow transplant, robotic cancer surgery and HIFU for prostate cancer, backed by PET-CT, PET-MR, 3T MRI and molecular diagnostics. Its cardiac programme includes angioplasty, bypass, valve repair, electrophysiology, hybrid cardiac surgery and heart-lung transplants, and the Fortis Institute of Robotic Surgery is a centre of excellence.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 280 beds, more than 150 doctors and 800 paramedical staff, with emergency care, organ transplants and preventive care.\n##international\nFortis Bannerghatta Road offers international patient services with medical visa assistance, translators and concierge support, and reports assisting patients from more than 175 countries. It is on Bannerghatta Road in south Bengaluru.",
	'aster-cmi-hospital':
		"##history\nAster CMI Hospital in Hebbal, Bengaluru, is part of Aster DM Healthcare, one of Asia's largest healthcare networks, operating across nine countries. Sources differ on its opening year, so it is best described as a hospital of the 2010s. It is accredited by NABH and NABL and has close to 500 beds, from primary to quaternary care. It was the first hospital in Bangalore to be chosen as the kidney transplant centre for the state of Karnataka, and it was the first in Karnataka to be certified by FPID (US) as a centre of excellence for primary immune deficiencies.\n##specialities\nAster CMI offers centres of excellence in cardiac sciences, neurosciences, gastroenterology, integrated liver care, organ transplant, urology and nephrology, orthopaedics, women's health and child and adolescent health, with more than 38 specialities under one roof. Its transplant programme has completed more than 1,000 kidney transplants in total, including 54 robotic kidney transplants so far, using the da Vinci surgical robot. The Aster International Institute of Oncology offers proton beam therapy, robotic surgery, HIPEC and molecular tumour profiling.\n##technology\nThe hospital is in the Hebbal area on the airport road, and its urology and nephrology department has been ranked among the best in Bangalore in the Times of India critical care survey.\n##international\nFor international patients, Aster CMI provides dedicated coordination, airport transfers, foreign-language interpreters and visa support. Hebbal is on the route between central Bengaluru and Kempegowda International Airport.",
	'apollo-hospitals-jubilee-hills':
		"##history\nApollo Hospitals, Jubilee Hills, established in 1988, is the flagship Apollo hospital in Hyderabad and holds JCI accreditation. It has been honoured by the Government of India as a premier medical tourism hospital and has received the FICCI Healthcare Excellence Award. It introduced India's first PET-CT scanner in 2005, performed India's first coronary angioplasty using a fully absorbable stent, and has performed more than 150,000 heart surgeries with a reported success rate above 99 percent. It has also completed more than 700 cochlear implants.\n##specialities\nThe hospital runs 12 centres of excellence. The cardiac sciences centre has three cath labs and dedicated cardiac operating theatres, with robotic-assisted cardiac surgery, TAVI and complex coronary interventions. The cancer centre draws on 35 years of experience and offers robotic onco-surgery. Neurosciences is equipped with an intra-operative MRI suite, neuro-navigation and spinal robotics. The transplant team handles liver, kidney, heart and bone marrow transplants, and the Apollo group has performed more than 43,000 organ transplants.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 550 beds and is accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL. It is on Road No. 72, Film Nagar, Jubilee Hills.\n##international\nThe hospital handles more than 800 international patient consultations a month, with patients from countries including the USA, UAE, Tanzania, Kenya and Oman. A dedicated International Patient Services team assists with medical visas, travel arrangements, accommodation and interpretation.",
	'continental-hospitals':
		"##history\nContinental Hospitals was founded in April 2013 by Dr. Guru N. Reddy in Hyderabad's Financial District (Nanakramguda, Gachibowli). It is a 585-bed hospital spread across 18 floors and 1.4 million square feet, accredited by JCI, NABH and NABL, and is India's first LEED-qualified super-speciality hospital, with green operation theatres and Level 3 NICU and PICU. It won the ASSOCHAM Award 2022 for India's Best Hospital in Technology Adoption.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers more than 50 specialities and is known for complex organ transplants, cardiac sciences, neurosciences, oncology, gastro sciences and orthopaedics. In April 2023 its team of surgeons, led by Dr. Pradeep Rachakonda under the guidance of Dr. Sudhir Srivastava, performed the first robot-assisted coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) surgery in India with the SSI Mantra robot. Its transplant department handles liver, kidney, heart, lung and bone marrow transplants, supported by advanced ICUs and post-transplant rehabilitation.\n##technology\nThe hospital has 16 modular green operation theatres and 90 single-room ICU beds, and surgeons trained in the da Vinci and other robotic platforms.\n##international\nContinental has a dedicated area for international patients and a health-check lounge. It is in the Financial District near Hyderabad's IT corridor, roughly 30 to 45 minutes from the airport.",
	'yashoda-hospitals-somajiguda':
		"##history\nYashoda Hospitals, Somajiguda, is the first hospital of the Yashoda Group and started in 1994, following a small clinic set up in 1989 by Dr. G. Surendar Rao. Over three decades the group has expanded to branches in Somajiguda, Secunderabad, Malakpet and Hitec City. The Somajiguda unit was recognised as a Patient Friendly Hospital by AHPI, and the group has been ranked first in cadaveric organ transplantation by the Government of India and first in multispecialty hospitals at the Times Healthcare Achievers awards.\n##specialities\nThe hospital has 400+ beds, around 250 doctors and 500 nurses. Its centres of excellence cover heart and CT surgery, neurosciences, cancer, liver and multi-organ transplants, bones and joints, nephrology, robotic sciences, spine surgery, mother and child care and fertility, along with a very wide list of departments from ENT and gynaecology to plastic surgery, nuclear medicine and bariatric surgery. The group's transplant milestones include the first lung transplant in the Telugu states (2012) and a combined heart-lung transplant (2017).\n##technology\nLaboratory, diagnostic services and pharmacy operate around the clock. The hospital is NABH accredited and is the first in the region to introduce robotic surgery.\n##international\nYashoda offers international patient services, with its transplant programme ranking among India's top multi-organ programmes and a multidisciplinary team for dialysis, liver and kidney disease and paediatric transplants. Somajiguda is on Raj Bhavan Road in central Hyderabad.",
	'global-hospitals-hyderabad':
		"##history\nGleneagles Global Hospitals at Lakdi-ka-pul, known as Global Hospitals, was the first Gleneagles Global hospital opened in Hyderabad and belongs to the Global Hospitals Group, founded in 1999 by Dr. K. Ravindranath. It pioneered the first heart transplant in the erstwhile states of Andhra Pradesh and Telangana, performed the region's first bone marrow transplant and the first twin kidney transplant, and reports India's first successful split and auxiliary liver transplant. It was ranked second-best multi-specialty hospital in Hyderabad and among the top 10 in South India in a 2021 Times of India survey.\n##specialities\nThe hospital is known for liver, kidney, heart and lung transplants, and also offers hepatology, nephrology, bariatrics, gastroenterology, multi-organ transplants, aesthetic and reconstructive surgery, oncology, cardiac sciences, paediatrics, psychiatry, endocrinology, ENT, orthopaedics, spine surgery, gastro sciences, general and laparoscopic surgery and pulmonology.\n##technology\nThe hospital has about 150 beds and six operation theatres, with robotic and minimal-access capability, and multiple ICUs including a surgical ICU, CT-ICU, step-down ICU, liver ICU and post-transplant units. It is accredited by NABH and NABL.\n##international\nThe hospital offers international patient support through the Gleneagles Global group. Lakdi-ka-pul is a central Hyderabad location near Lakdi-ka-pul Metro station.",
	'kims-hospitals-secunderabad':
		"##history\nKIMS Hospitals, Secunderabad, opened in 2004 as the flagship hospital of the Krishna Institute of Medical Sciences group, a 1,000-bed tertiary and quaternary-care hospital, one of the largest private hospitals in India. The group was founded in 2000 by cardio-thoracic surgeon Dr. Bhaskar Rao Bollineni, who has performed more than 30,000 surgeries over 25 years and was instrumental in formulating the Rajiv Gandhi Aarogyasri scheme in 2007. The group now has more than two dozen hospitals, and its executive director and CEO is Dr. Abhinay Bollineni.\n##specialities\nThe hospital offers more than 25 specialities and super-specialities, including cardiology, gastroenterology and hepatology, neurosciences, organ transplantation, oncology, orthopaedics, urology, fertility, renal sciences and mother and child care. Its neurosciences centre handles brain tumours, spinal deformities, deep brain stimulation for Parkinson's disease and stroke management, and the KIMS Advanced Gastroenterology and Endoscopy (KAGE) centre treats complex digestive disorders, liver diseases and POEM procedures.\n##technology\nThe transplant programme covers heart, lung, liver, kidney and bone marrow, including advanced ex-vivo perfusion. The heart and lung transplant centre completed its first heart transplant in 2012 and performs about 75 heart and lung transplants each year, and the hospital recorded 1,000 kidney transplants in 2019. It is accredited by NABH and holds ISO 9001:2015 certification.\n##international\nKIMS Secunderabad is on Minister Road in central Secunderabad, close to Secunderabad railway station.",
};
